{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5","id":1543084,"title":"A Legacy Fan Finally Reads W5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-03T22:01:49-07:00","id":1543084,"title":"A Legacy Fan Finally Reads W5","content":"Well, the first chapter was a slog. I wonder what the Gifts are like...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf 5th edition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hart Wardens...<br /> Blessed Brew<br /> Balor's Gaze</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lh_W6FLaMvA\" data-code=\"Lh_W6FLaMvA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Lh_W6FLaMvA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Some mighty fine reimagination of the concept, Lou.<br /> <br /> (I'm coming back to this. Just consider it time to properly warm up the shards of glass and fireplace implements.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T18:03:01-07:00","id":1543129,"title":"","content":"I'm going to dig into some Gifts now. I feel the need to preface this by noting that I never really felt great about the widespread use of perma-Renown values in W:tA Gifts, being fairly comfy in the weird and off the wall Trait combinations that you saw (Manipulation + Craft to convince a bunch of machines that they shouldn't work!), so Gifts using Attribute + Renown, especially when it's only three types of Renown and some may or may not fit, irk me by default. Adding on the lack of Gnosis and focus on Rage, and you just have too few variables to work with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>W5</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Native Gifts</div> </div> </div> </div>Because we'd rather not even remember lupus Garou. And Crinos-born? HAH!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Renown 1 </div> </div> </div>The equivalent of starter-tier stuff, even though &quot;starter-tier&quot; in W:tA had a lot more to do with spiritual attunement and favor, i.e. the reason that Rokea got Teeth of the Skin at Rank 1 instead of 4, or why Bastet could all be counted on to have the really boss Catfeet Gift at Rank 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Catfeet </div> </div> </div>Well, that kind of takes the wind from the sails of the Bastet... not that the people in charge probably care.<br /> <br /> Works in any form, keeps you from slipping without a roll, ignores fall damage under a certain height, can be activated reflexively... but requires 1 Willpower. A bit of a nerf, since it doesn't aid in a bunch of other balance-related rolls like grappling. I suppose it could have been worse; the tenor of a lot of Gifts is that some assmad Vampire stan got really vengeful reworking stuff, even if it was way subtler than, say, anything that altered Crinos to be more effective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eyes of the Owl </div> </div> </div>Your eyes glow and you can see in the da... come on, guys. This is blatantly just Protean 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hare's Leap </div> </div> </div>Your jumping distance is now based on Strength + Glory, but at least it didn't get driven into the ground.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Penumbral Senses </div> </div> </div>Basically, you're straddling the gauntlet. Spirits can see you if you're physical but you're still invisible to physical beings if you're using it in the Umbra. Past editions did this largely via peaking, a natural ability that Garou just had.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Raging Strike </div> </div> </div>You can... add your Glory to your unarmed attack pool for one Rage check? This is like a meaner version of Trick Shot for mauling people. Again, it seems like the Vampire stans didn't like the less direct approach for a lot of Gifts and just added on some kind of Celerity effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Staredown </div> </div> </div>You don't need to roll against non-magical humans, they just beat it, but other games' characters and such get to resist. Can't be used if anyone started swinging first, which is a nerf, as is only getting one shot at it. Fortunately, not so nerfed that you have to be out of Homid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Total Renown 4 </div> </div> </div>Intermediate for this category, in other words.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sharpened Senses </div> </div> </div>Blanket reduction of difficulty for sensory rolls, but it costs one Willpower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spirit of the Fray </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wdfLr97nblE\" data-code=\"wdfLr97nblE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/wdfLr97nblE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> A kind of poster child for how the Vampire hardliners for crossover Do Not Get It, this Gift's effects in W5 are what every Garou could use Rage to do to make multiple attacks, limited by Dex and Wits. Except that you can only get in one attack per target, so no straight-up mauling one dude with a vengeance. Each extra attack requires a Rage check. The only silver lining is that if you used something like Raging Strike, it applies to every attack.<br /> <br /> This is a huge nerf, because in addition to this being a basic part of Rage, Spirit of the Fray also used to let you either go first (pre-Revised) or likely beat the Initiative count. Did it make Garou really dangerous to attack? Yes, but in those days, it was also mostly limited to Ahrouns (others could get it for a higher price), and also who cares unless you're trying to one up the Garou in a combat game, which is just flat out a losing proposition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thwarting the Arrow </div> </div> </div>Only usable in Crinos, it makes projectiles curve away from you. Still not a consolation for anything, really, as you need to be as preoccupied with Honor as Prince Zuko in order to really make it work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Total Renown 7 </div> </div> </div>Top of the world, ma! But not really, as you'll soon see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Body Shift </div> </div> </div>You know that weird Gift from the 1e player's guide that allowed you to change your Physical Attributes? It's that, plus Rat Head. Given the limits of how many dots you can move around, I'm not sure why this is the equivalent of an elder-tier power, except that the power balance of this game doesn't actually exist and it was pointless to take Rage extra actions away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Jam Technology </div> </div> </div>Getting really transparent that the Vampire crowd hated some effects here. Not only is it reliant on following in the footsteps of Zuko for some reason, it also won't let you keep sharp objects from cutting. Given that it also calls out bicycles as being really difficult to use it on, I can't help but think that they were trying to enforce some kind of safety rule for a Kids on Bikes crossover. The only saving grace is that it lasts for an entire scene, which was way longer than it did in past editions, but at what cost?<br /> <br /> (Also, its description is functionally the same as in past editions and it has the same misleading name. Reboot or reimagination, my ass!)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tongue of the Beasts </div> </div> </div>&quot;You are now friends with a stick bug. The stick bug will now DIE FOR YOU.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's but one example use given for being able to communicate with non-human animals, but it's kind of weird that it was. This is also starting to burrow beneath the surface of the mindset that no one should have when writing W:tA but numerous authors clearly did for this book, where it starts to discount animal cognitive faculties because in addition to not having read any W:tA books since 1993, I can't imagine that they read up on anything about comparative cognition more recent than the 80s. I know it's common for trpgs, but again, for Werewolf, it's jarring in the extreme, since it generally doesn't posture about human cognitive capabilities. That would ruin the atmosphere of the entire game.<br /> <br /> Time to go and do something else. I'll be back tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-06-2024, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T22:45:03-07:00","id":1543138,"title":"","content":"Check out sharpened senses if you REALLY want to cry. You get HUMAN senses in lupus form XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T23:38:23-07:00","id":1543139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1543138#post1543138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check out sharpened senses if you REALLY want to cry. You get HUMAN senses in lupus form XD</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. But as bad as that is, there's worse yet waiting in the wings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T02:00:15-07:00","id":1543141,"title":"","content":"The spirit of the frey thing tickles me a little. It really does feel like some sort of private grudge, like trying to make it hard to gank the prince in the umbra. I recall having a completly asinine discussion with a fanboy about how he could beat all mages with it.<br /> <br /> Jokes on the vampire fanboys, their powers are so objectively 'meh' spirits still probably better lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T02:45:52-07:00","id":1543143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1543129#post1543129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;You are now friends with a stick bug. The stick bug will now DIE FOR YOU.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's but one example use given for being able to communicate with non-human animals, but it's kind of weird that it was. This is also starting to burrow beneath the surface of the mindset that no one should have when writing W:tA but numerous authors clearly did for this book, where it starts to discount animal cognitive faculties because in addition to not having read any W:tA books since 1993, I can't imagine that they read up on anything about comparative cognition more recent than the 80s. I know it's common for trpgs, but again, for Werewolf, it's jarring in the extreme, since it generally doesn't posture about human cognitive capabilities. That would ruin the atmosphere of the entire game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically from a bunch of Scandinavian writers, W5 is not interested in nature. It is not interested in animal life or the idea that humans aren't the Most Important Species Ever. W5 has as much interest in the natural world as V5 has. As in, how it might serve the PCs. To W5, nature has no inherent value if the PCs don't give it any. Even the wolf born's family members are simply animals and so they are unfit for Touchstones beyond a single one that is assumed to die soon anyway.<br /> <br /> Nature in W5 exists Outside. It exists as the unknowable and alien. Not as part of the PCs and a reminder what they are fighting for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T00:27:30-07:00","id":1543188,"title":"","content":"Ragabash Gifts!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Total Renown 2 </div> </div> </div>The required Renown is higher for Auspices. These are still the basement level, first of three.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blissful Ignorance </div> </div> </div>This one is coming a bit earlier, unless your mindset is to compact pairs of ranks together. Oddly enough, still requires Stealth if you plan on waiting for an ambush. Also requires Wisdom to be really effective, which is another count of &quot;Wouldn't this be better if you had, I don't know, Cunning and another type of Renown?&quot; because that's a bit of an odd fit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Crow's Laughter </div> </div> </div>This one is even more off - a troll laugh that's supernaturally difficult to ignore and directs all attention toward you. For some reason, it requires HONOR! (I'm going to be hitting this Ember Island Zuko thing a lot, sorry not sorry). Causes Emotional Damage (Superficial to WP).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gremlins </div> </div> </div>This one is even earlier than Blissful Ignorance, and at first seems more effective than the older version of the Gift in some ways, as it has a five meter reach. However, your dice pool is going to be... markedly different. Better farm that Glory, cub. Also requires a critical success to perma-brick something, and it's trimmed back in the way that Jam Technology was, so overall, not great, but not the worst change that a Gift has had coming to W5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spider's Song </div> </div> </div>A lot of this text is copied wholesale from the W20 entry. Nerfed here, as it requires a Resolve + Wisdom roll to listen in, and a fair number of successes to actually hear everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Total Renown 5 </div> </div> </div>Intermediate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blur of the Milky Eye </div> </div> </div>This one clocks in a lot later, as it used to be an intro Gift. This one is odd, in that it is a stealth Gift that requires a Rage check to use. Yet another reason that Gnosis is really needed. Now functions to make you like the Predator, but only until you actually attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Open Seal </div> </div> </div>Vampire main bitterness, rising. Also a former intro Gift, now relies on HONOR! and makes opening mystically protected doors way harder. Stay mad, vamps; odds are you'll miss something important!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pulse of the Prey </div> </div> </div>Now requires a resource expenditure and works on Death Note rules. Nerfed, clearly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Scent of Running Water </div> </div> </div>One gets the distinct impression that Vampire and Werewolf had really, really different priorities in how they rated powers. Hmm. Who would have thought. At any rate, this eliminates all traces of your passage and makes you harder to track via Renown, so it's kind of buffed a little, particularly in being able to bring your pack along for the ride.<br /> <br /> Crucially, though it can be used in Lupus and is turned on or off at will, there is no callout made that you need to have it off to meaningfully interact with wolves. Probably because as has been pointed out, they don't think that's possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Total Renown 8 </div> </div> </div>Elder level, I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Luna's Blessing </div> </div> </div>Major nerf. Requires activation and doesn't protect against all silver damage, nor does it add those extra three dice that are only there to provide 1s. Quelle surprise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thieving Talons of the Magpie </div> </div> </div>Some of the pools get shifted around, and the Renown doesn't make sense (HONOR!), but the core of the power remains. WTF? I've heard more rants about this one than any other, bar none, but apparently it got the pass. Did not see that one coming.<br /> <br /> Also, it refers to the level of a Gift as its Rank, which is not how Gifts seem to be referred to anywhere else. Ah, eto... bleh!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Thousand Forms </div> </div> </div>Another bizarre dice pool and questionable Renown choice, and you can't turn into mythical animals. Nerfed. Also doesn't account for being able to turn into an animal that could be much, much better at communicating with humans than a wolf (if you turn into a parrot, you can utterly fuck with someone's head for fairly obvious reasons, and they're far from the only animal with a talent for vocal mimicry). Once again, kind of predictable; woe for the loss of writers chosen for knowledge of, you know, the natural world that the Garou are fighting for, and everything living within it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whelp Body </div> </div> </div>A nerf in some ways, since its range is rather truncated and it uses HONOR! for some reason. Some maniac got rid of the &quot;only used once per target ever&quot; part, though, so even if its effects aren't permanent, it can be heinously spammed without mercy. So, if you're playing W5 as a Ragabash, make sure to do just that. You'll need to commit to the ideals of both Prince Zuko and Kiryuin Satsuki to make it functional, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T02:54:13-07:00","id":1543192,"title":"","content":"Two general notes on Gifts in W5:<ul><li>For most Gifts you have to be in a supernatural Form (Glabro, Crinos or Hispo) to use them. What this means is that you not only have the Rage-check for the Gift (or the WP-cost) but you also have to deal with the one (or two in the case of Crinos) Rage-check for shifting Form. In addition, in W5 you not only have to do the Rage-check for shifting Form but you need to do the Rage-check <i>again </i>for every scene afterwards. So a lot of Gifts are tied to being in a supernatural Form when at the same time W5 as a game discourages shifting often and for too long. There are a lot of Gifts with smaller effects (like Eyes of the Owl or Penumbral Senses) where it feels like a waste to tie it to having to be in a supernatural Form. And it feels like unnecessary word-count bloat to have to add &quot;This Gift can be used in any Form.&quot; to the Gift-descriptions.</li> <li>The Renown-distribution is one of those things where you could have made it work with the three Renowns by giving the Gift-list a full overhaul instead of trying to crowbar old Gifts into this framework, I think. Also, the way it's presented it feels weird that the Tribe Gifts are tied to one Renown while Native- and Auspice-Gifts try to be balanced in what Renown is called for. That way it makes it seem like Tribe is the main-indicator of what Renown you're gonna focus on rather than your Auspice.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T00:43:32-07:00","id":1543257,"title":"","content":"THEURGE!<br /> <br /> Beginner's Level!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ensnare Spirit </div> </div> </div>Apparently taught by a filthy, filthy Weaver-spirit of law, this Gift mentions mandates that Gaia gave in a mythic time. And to use it, you need HONOR! to keep the spirit at bay. But if it already attacked, you're SOL. It gives a slight penalty to the spirit's rolls, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mother's Touch </div> </div> </div>Glory? Seriously? If that isn't the best case for Succor needing to be a fourth or fifth category of Renown, I don't know what is. Oh, and it heals boring, starchy, ham-filled superficial damage. Costs WP instead of Gnosis, and healing is more effective if your patient has less Rage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shadow Sense </div> </div> </div>Basically, it's Sense the Unnatural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sight From Beyond </div> </div> </div>Still based on the ST's whims. The more things change...<br /> <br /> Intermediate!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Banish Spirit </div> </div> </div>Huh. It's way, way easier to kick banes out of fomori, now. The damage is substantially less, especially if you get a good roll on this Gift. Which requires Glory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Grasp From Beyond </div> </div> </div>Bypass the time-based Umbral travel damage by pulling your car into the spirit world!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mindspeak </div> </div> </div>Now, I know what you might be thinking. &quot;But isn't that a Galliard Gift?&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes. It was. You can probably already guess the scourge that has overcome the Galliard Gifts. At any rate, this Gift has been nerfed heavily in some capacities, as it no longer allows groups, but you don't have to be in line of sight unless you don't know the target. It's also impossible to multi-task and act with your real body without breaking the Gift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Umbral Tether </div> </div> </div>Pretty much the way it was, except, you know, for not being entry-level. Also gives a bonus for navigation. The book keeps referring to the Umbra as the Spirit Wilds, incidentally, and I don't like it.<br /> <br /> Elder Level!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Command Spirit </div> </div> </div>In spite of being higher in tier, it still can't force a spirit out of what it's possessed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Drain Spirit </div> </div> </div>Not much has changed, except that they won't even give an Essence rating to spirits. Also, kind of weird to use Glory. Unlike past editions, explicitly called out as that one little trick that spirits hate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Feral Regression </div> </div> </div>I guess it wouldn't do to keep calling it Feral Lobotomy. At any rate, much like Whelp Body, the book really doesn't want to cause permanent damage, so you'll likely only end up wrecking their faculties for the remainder of the story. Also targets Mental Attributes in general instead of Intelligence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Living Ward </div> </div> </div>THE LIVING WARD! MWA HAHAHAHAHA! [/The Critic Version of Orson Welles]<br /> <br /> If I'm comparing this to Spirit Ward, it's way more limited in its exclusion radius and doesn't auto-damage spirits in said radius. With noticeable backfire potential, it's a big nerf.<br /> <br /> And that's it; no Pulse of the Invisible, no Malleable Spirit, no Ultimate Argument of Logic, definitely no As In The Beginning. Not really surprising; if diehard Vampire partisans are aching to nerf anything, it would be the Garou capacity to interact with the Umbra and deal with spirits. How dare those characters in the other game do something better in such a clear manner?<br /> <br /> Next time, we're going to start catching the text in a blatant, bald-faced lie with the Philodox Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T19:16:14-07:00","id":1543315,"title":"","content":"Philodox- Keeper of the Ways. What Ways? Look in a pre-W5 book!<br /> <br /> Beginner Level<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ancestral Conviction </div> </div> </div>Now, W5 beats the &quot;Garou are worthless and have nothing to help outside of a fight&quot; drum more often than Exalted: the Lunars beat its &quot;we don't need no Solar Exalted, we don't need no social control&quot; drum. This Gift cuts against that notion by allowing you to add your HONOR! to Persuasion against other Garou. Why is this significant? Because it means that the Philodox can actually iron out disputes, in spite of the assumption of the writing that no one can even try to keep the folks around them from going to shit. The text is saying one thing while the rules are going in the opposite direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gaia's Candor </div> </div> </div>It's Truth of Gaia. It uses Glory. Why? Degenerate game states.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Porcupine's Reprisal </div> </div> </div>It's the Justice Field from Red Dwarf. It also uses Glory, and does superficial damage as an auto-hit counterattack effect. For some reason, even though its name mentions it, the first example spirit to teach it is a hedgehog-spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sense the True Form </div> </div> </div>Someone decided that Scent wasn't evocative and went with a general-use Sense. It's a lot harder to tell if someone is a non-Werewolf, and it costs WP, continuing in the baffling trend of &quot;this was free to use in prior editions, but will cost you now.&quot;<br /> <br /> Intermediate Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beast's Fealty </div> </div> </div>It's King of Beasts. Except that King of Beasts didn't go out of its way to highlight another case of &quot;This animal will die for you.&quot; What do the writers think we are? Animalism-using licks?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Command the Gathering </div> </div> </div>Yet another case where the Garou do, in fact, have ways to convince and sway others, in this case, crowds of them. Can't be used if violence breaks out, but no one can say that you didn't at least try.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fangs of Judgment </div> </div> </div>Instead of being a combat Charm for use against beings that broke the laws of Gaia, it marks a single enemy for death and gives a +1 damage bonus. Seems kind of paltry for an intermediate Gift in the hands of someone how can already dish out huge gobs of damage, probably, but it does last until the enemy is dead and benefits your entire pack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Scent of the Past </div> </div> </div>Psychometric visions of a location. Except that since this game wants to ignore the past where it pertains to Garou and their society, it's highly limited and can't reach back for more than a few years. Weaksauce; most Gifts that were mid-tier in past editions could reach back way farther than that.<br /> <br /> Elder Level Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Geas </div> </div> </div>&quot;I, Lelouch vi Britannia, command you to sign all your shares in the company away to this trust...&quot;<br /> <br /> For some reason, it can't get people to tell you information. Which I guess is just another count on the great, big &quot;I dunno!&quot; of the entire edition's backstory. Since the effective duration of this Gift is truncated down to a scene and it can only hit one person at a time, I feel confident saying that this is horribly nerfed, and I could also be extremely uncharitable and suggest it was because Vampire mains don't like it when Garou mind-whammy their characters instead of the other way around.<br /> <br /> That aside, another example of how Garou do, in fact, have tools to use for non-violent ends. Perhaps you won't have the roller coaster ride of world domination that Lelouch did in Code Geass spamming it whenever you can, but you'll probably be able to deal some terrible blows to organizations by getting close to their decision makers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oathbreaker's Bane </div> </div> </div>Great for a contingency, but it doesn't do much to magically punish breaking an oath; it's merely an assurance that you know when it happens and where they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Take the True Form </div> </div> </div>No one shapeshifts in front of Zuko. The opposed roll means that you might not be able to make it work, though, so boo! Boo! Boo!<br /> <br /> The Philodoxes made out well, as far as anyone did, but the book seems to think that their Gifts don't exist, or somehow could never possibly change the world, even though this is some pretty nice social power. Yet another reason that you should probably just scrap whatever they have planned and refer to the history in Revised. Tomorrow, we'll delve into the terrible fate of the Galliard auspice in W5. I guarantee that if you know about the writing background for sample Galliard characters, you absolutely will not be surprised in the slightest.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T07:36:31-07:00","id":1543337,"title":"","content":"I think what we are seeing here is another aspect of the rush W5 was made in. The book says a lot, but the core gameplay loop has not actually changed much. Only some powers have been nerfed or vamp-ed rather.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T12:05:01-07:00","id":1543354,"title":"","content":"And some powers that were similar to a particular manifestation of Presence no longer are. But that's several splats down.<br /> <br /> Galliard Gifts<br /> <br /> The first part of Galliard Gifts goes on to describe... Song Gifts! You can only be using one song at a time! Because Galliards are artists which means music and being musicians. No historians could ever possibly be in this splat. Oh no.<br /> <br /> Beginner Level<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Animal Magnetism </div> </div> </div>Shit name of the power I'd always wished they'd remove or seriously alter. But here, it's just a fairly solid social boost, which is yet another strike against the supposition of &quot;Garou do not have the tools for dealing with people outside of violence&quot;.<br /> <br /> Because they do. It adds to all social pools for a scene. I wonder if they'll ever address that in whatever books might come.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Howl of Assembly </div> </div> </div>This is like Strength of Will from legacy, which was an elder-level Ahroun Gift. But here, it can only give back a single point of WP and can only be used once per session. Sad Zuko noises.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Song of Rage </div> </div> </div>Gives a point or two of Rage once per session. This is a stark departure from its prior form, where it would just get anyone - even if they couldn't normally frenzy - to potentially lose their shit and frenzy. Wonderful for making sure that your enemies couldn't employ coordinated actions in combat. Here? It's just turning Galliards into helpful bards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Song of Serenity </div> </div> </div>Literally the opposite of Song of Rage in function, and can also pull someone out of frenzy. Clear evidence that Song of Rage should make people frenzy, though it doesn't.<br /> <br /> Intermediate Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Call the Ridden </div> </div> </div>Since W5 is extremely non-committal about the Wyrm being bad for some reason, Call of the Wyrm got turned into just attracting possessed characters. For some reason, no longer uses Manipulation. It does use HONOR!, which seems like yet another case for Cunning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eyes of the Cobra </div> </div> </div>Aside from the pluralizing of its name and the dice pool used, pretty much the same thing as Eye of the Cobra. I guess ChaGlo works well enough. There's also a weird subsystem for not looking into someone's eyes; I guess you could use that to avoid Dominate, too. Since it ends when your quarry gets there but can last for an entire scene, you can potentially keep falling back just a bit to get them into dangerous situations that Call the Ridden wouldn't, and it works on anyone with functional eyes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Song of Valor </div> </div> </div>Tell me, Mr. Anderson, how will you sing of the deeds of ancient Garou heroes... if you have no idea what they are? Assuming that your character actually has material to work with, they can expand the rerolling via Willpower system for everyone for the scene. Can only be used once per d- I mean session. Certainly Galliards are not blatantly just bards!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Song of Inspiration </div> </div> </div>&quot;Okay, you got us. Galliards are totally just D&amp;D bards for Garou.&quot;<br /> <br /> No use restriction, too, so you really can just go around playing music for inspiring your pack members just like Elan from OOTS.<br /> <br /> &quot;Elder&quot; Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Against the Odds </div> </div> </div>Oh, now here's Strength of Will!... but only for your pack, and only once per story. It's nerf or nothin'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Break the Shackles </div> </div> </div>Formerly a legendary Gift that also allowed you to free others from being physically restrained, now just for breaking mind control. I suppose we're lucky it even does that, but the fact that there's an ST-ruled, arbitrary difficulty for doing so based on the power of the one that initiated control doesn't bode well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Defy Death </div> </div> </div>Ah, see, now here's how to nerf a power! For reference, the Silver Fangs' secret of death, Ignore Wound, allowed them to flat out ignore a killing blow. This? This slightly cushions it by allowing you to roll your HONOR! to try and claw back from the edge of death. Given dice probability, I think you'll end up dying if you try to use this even once... just like my incredibly unfortunate Flagellants in Darkest Dungeon on the first Death's Door. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7rM90_r8G7k\" target=\"_blank\">[OMINOUS BELL TONE]</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dreamwalk </div> </div> </div>Like Gift of Dreams, but surprisingly improved in a number of ways, as you can peep on peoples' dreams as well and you're not limited by distance or the need to breathe dreams into someone. A rare win, here.<br /> <br /> So, now you know why practically all the Galliard characters in the books are musicians - someone seemed to literally think that &quot;Galliard = D&amp;D Bard&quot; and wrote it into their mechanics. There was no time for historians; if you can't play music, you can't be a D&amp;D bard! Except that not even D&amp;D bards are that restricted, I think. So you're really more like a caricature of one, with some combat leadership that used to be the Ahroun's bag. Which probably raises a justifiably terrifying question - if the Ahrouns aren't inspiring others to fight anymore, what do they do?<br /> <br /> (Combat and scaring people. It's mostly just combat and scaring people.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-08-2024, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T15:17:49-07:00","id":1543361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1543354#post1543354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that not even D&amp;D bards are that restricted, I think. So you're really more like a caricature of one</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to say, you're right.<br /> <br /> Despite popular belief/renditions, D&amp;D Bard is actually far more than music. And a lot of them are Historians, by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T07:55:57-07:00","id":1543425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1543138#post1543138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check out sharpened senses if you REALLY want to cry. You get HUMAN senses in lupus form XD</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose color vision would come in handy if you need to defuse a bomb while in lupus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T23:29:14-07:00","id":1543495,"title":"","content":"Ahroun, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eGslweDOihs\" target=\"_blank\">56709</a>.<br /> <br /> We're given a text box for Claw Gifts. They have the same restrictions as Song Gifts, but for claws. Someone hated power stacking something fierce.<br /> <br /> Beginner Level - Whoopsie Doodle, the book lists it as Renown 1 like the Native Gifts!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Halt the Coward's Flight </div> </div> </div>This is very informative, in that the design staff that settled on this thought that being an Ahroun was so synonymous with being a Get of Fenris, that they had less work to do rather than more to emphasize the distinction between the tribe and the auspice. In any case, this Gift is very similar to a Fenrir one of prior days, and it at least makes sense for it to use HONOR!, I suppose. It's slightly more effective here, believe it or not, because it slows down targets way more than by half and can slow down vehicles. I'm not sure that the staff really thought that one through, but I'll take it, such as it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rapid Shift </div> </div> </div>This really should be a Native Gift. And not have a horrible potential drawback (damage if you miss the roll by the number of missing successes). Or maybe you should just put Primal-Urge back in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Razor Claws </div> </div> </div>Almost as impressive as the W20 version, this slow-trickles damage buff in the form of relying on your Glory, but not like, all of it. Also causes you to grow claws in forms that don't have claw attacks, so it basically also packages in Predator's Arsenal, if you squint. Doesn't explicitly say that it works in said forms, so it may have been that Gifts could originally be used in every form by default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sense Danger </div> </div> </div>Broadened from Sense Silver, I suppose. It's a perma-buff to your capabilities in case of immediate danger, so basically Spidey Sense.<br /> <br /> Intermediate Gifts (Correct Renown amount listed)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Primal Anger </div> </div> </div>Pretty much works as before, but it's a full tank up, since Rage is so low now. Also limited in use, probably because the game hates opportunities for you to use Rage and wants them to end in three turns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Snarl of Challenge </div> </div> </div>&quot;You dare to refuse my batchall? Prepare to feel the wrath of the Falcon's Claws!&quot;<br /> <br /> You're basically marking opponents like in D&amp;D 4e, here, and not with the one at a time powers, either. You get some temporary HLs if anyone that you succeeded against attacks you. At least one part of the auspice that's not &quot;Me smash! Me scary!&quot; still exists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True Fear </div> </div> </div>Norms shit bricks. Other monsters might shit bricks. Somewhat on par with its prior version, as it can be resisted, but rather expensively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wind Claws </div> </div> </div>Nerfed severely, because it doesn't completely ignore armor, doesn't do so well against magic armor, and can't be stacked with other Gifts that increase claw damage or the like.<br /> <br /> Elder Level Gifts (if that is their real name)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Closing the Gap </div> </div> </div>This is inferior to a Celerity 3 power, like, far behind it. Weaksauce, especially since I was hoping back in the day that Rage would just allow it without the need to get endgame-tier Gifts to focus on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kiss of Helios </div> </div> </div>Heavy nerf, since it doesn't do extra agg anymore (only a small amount of superficial to people who touch you). It does still protect you from heat and fire, but not nearly as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Luna's Armor </div> </div> </div>Only of use against silver or fire, rather than granting broad protection that includes special cases against silver, so it's kind of like a kneecapped version of itself combined with a kneecapped version of Master of Fire. As usual, consistency is not to be found and balance is a joke.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Silver Claws </div> </div> </div>A nerf so pointless that it cannot be properly expressed in writing, this does one agg to you per turn, and it takes a roll to fight through the pain each turn to keep it active instead of, you know, providing Rage. I don't really get why this is end-tier when Unstoppable Warrior exists, but I guess that's certainly never something that we're going to see. I'm not sure that I can ascribe Vampire main writers being mad about it, either, since it has jack all to do with threatening anyone but other Garou and most Fera. That's why it was a step up in legacy, but not the end of the line.<br /> <br /> (The same really applies to Crinos; it is no end to the path, merely the beginning of being able to utilize the power of incredible violence.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-10-2024, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T01:15:39-07:00","id":1543573,"title":"","content":"Tribal Gifts! Tribes, now no longer associated with specific human cultures!<br /> <br /> Beginning Gifts (Requires 3 Renown)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Curse of Aeolus </div> </div> </div>Well, that certainly didn't take long. Just like with the <s>Fianna</s> Hart Wardens. Much as with many other Gifts, they skipped ahead to get to some of what the writers presumably considered iconic, but without the capacity to tap into or detect the energies of the Triat, that makes a short footrace to making magic fog. As you might have guessed, it has also been nerfed, as it only covers the size of a single house instead of a city block (roughly 400 by 400 in feet). Awkwardly uses Glory, because of course it's the height of Glory to conceal your actions under a thick fog. Also, instead of being reliable soft cover, it is, much like every other Gift that inflicts a penalty, only a -2 to ranged attacks.<br /> <br /> Tribes also begin to just stretch the availability of auspice Gifts that we've seen. The other two beginniner Gifts for the Furies are Porcupine's Reprisal and... Halt the Coward's Flight.<br /> <br /> A Get of Fenris Gift in the Black Furies list? It's like a joke from a John Biles parody from the 90s that leans heavily on Ranma 1/2. Is anyone else old enough to get that? Google the Year of Projects, maybe it's still around.<br /> <br /> Intermediate Gifts (Tribe requires Renown 6)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Coup de Grace </div> </div> </div>Instead of easily just doubling the damage of an attack, it adds damage... but only if you would already bring their Health down to nada. I think this could have been done far, far better, but that pretty much goes without saying at this point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kali's Scar </div> </div> </div>Prevents a wound from healing for a night and a day, or not if the ST decides that the opponent is too powerful. Also allows you to track the target.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wasp Talons </div> </div> </div>At least this one still works. Also works in any form, oddly enough. The attack roll is a bit odd, but not nearly as odd as it could have been. The damage to your claws is superficial, so it can still be healed quickly to &quot;reload&quot;. The one flaw? No range mentioned.<br /> <br /> &quot;Elder&quot; Level Gifts - Renown 9, bucko.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gorgon's Visage </div> </div> </div>(Puts hand in shape of L) LAME! Bigtime lame. Barely manages to stop targets from moving, can't even turn them to stone, and is so telegraphed that anyone can look away quickly. Authors, chief editor, WTF do you think &quot;elder level&quot; is supposed to be?<br /> <br /> Furies also get Break the Shackles and Drain Spirit at this level.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also Whelp Body, but it can be hard to see given the flow of the text, if you flip rapidly between pages. This is somewhat close to getting Body Wrack, I guess.<br /> <br /> Because Tribes are so truncated in length, I'm fitting in another two.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers<br /> <br /> Beginner Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Odious Aroma </div> </div> </div>Gives you a Stink Aura that prevents others from touching you... based on your HONOR! Now, instead of a potential distraction in combat, it's apparently meant to stop combat, somehow.<br /> <br /> The Gnawers also get the previously-described Gifts of Blissful Ignorance, Rapid Shift, and Sight From Beyond.<br /> <br /> Intermediate Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Face in the Crowd </div> </div> </div>Lose people by entering a crowd of humans or canids. The Gift says dogs, but the book knows jack all about wolves or how they look, so I'm going to call shenanigans on that one. Relies on HONOR! for some reason (make Cunning a thing already! UGH!)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Streets Tell Stories </div> </div> </div>Literally put your ear to the street and hear anything going on along it or the buildings adjacent to it. Only living beings can be heard, so you'll only get half of a conversation over the phone. The combination of traits once again makes me imagine Satsuki and Prince Zuko trying to hear something while pressing their ears to the ground.<br /> <br /> Gnawers also have Scent of the Past available. This is all shaping up to be a bit too much emphasis on being the information-gatherers and brokers of the Garou, aka &quot;We read about<br /> urban werewolves in the dregs of the city and just assumed they would be like the Nosferatu&quot;.<br /> <br /> Elder Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Thousand Eyes </div> </div> </div>Talk about redundant. A bunch of Gifts for seeing and investigating around, turning the Gnawers into one-note Nosferatu clones wearing the &quot;I know secrets&quot; hat. Wait, let me amend that, &quot;I know secrets, and also rant about HONOR! like Zuko&quot; hat, because guess what Renown you need here? Mentions that you can see out of animals' eyes as long as they're cockroach sized, which is a failure of a balm for their patron shift. Basically, just an Animalism power in the Gnawer Gift list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Between the Cracks </div> </div> </div>This is using the name of a Gift that let you find a temporary bolthole but the effect of Blink, except that instead of shaded urban areas you're literally vanishing where one thing is cracked and exiting where there's another crack. Massively truncated in effective range as this one is, I'd rather have Blink, of course.<br /> <br /> The other elder Gnawer Gift is Defy Death which, as we've established, really should be in quotes for how unreliable it theoretically is.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia<br /> <br /> Given the Revised Tribebook, one shudders to imagine what cruel and inhuman indignities the Coggies will be subjected to.<br /> <br /> Beginner Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Brother's Scent </div> </div> </div>Yet another Gift for hiding in a crowd! The original explicitly mentioned that your presentation could be way, way off; no real hint of that, here. Only that you have to roll if someone is looking for people specifically. Also mentions the CoG as being an... impostor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sbHvogpfwro\" data-code=\"sbHvogpfwro\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/sbHvogpfwro/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> That's the only new Gift that they get. The others are Mother's Touch, Song of Serenity (does this mean that Coggies are compulsory musicians, too?), and Sense the True Form. They really didn't want to add in anything for variety, did they?<br /> <br /> Intermediate Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Calm the Furious Beast </div> </div> </div>Yet another concept wrecker for the supposed dismal state of the Garou, as you can pull someone out of a frenzy fairly easily. A bit harder to get than a beginner Gift, but still not locked behind Elder exclusivity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reveal Trauma </div> </div> </div>Like Diagnostics, but can also affect the living. Now that's some major league splitting and dilution of themes! No Pain Chain for you! While being able to diagnose any ailment or structural strain would sound nice, it only provides a bonus of two dice and not anything else.<br /> <br /> CoG also get Open Seal here.<br /> <br /> Elder Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Life's Presence </div> </div> </div>You can sense any living being, or undead feigning life, in... the area of two-story building. Conceptually, most similar to Song of the Earth Mother, which just blows this out of the water. It's not even funny how limited Life's Presence is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Share the Pain </div> </div> </div>Actually pretty nice, for once, as you can take injuries for your packmates. You can even change health level damage to Emotional Damage. Goes particularly well with Luna's Armor, which they also get here.<br /> <br /> (Break!)<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers got pretty heavily shafted here, because the direction was to make them Wolferatu, or as far as they're imagining, Dogsferatu. Nothing like Riot or Call the Rust that take them from being &quot;eyes on the street&quot; to wielding all the powers of the overlooked urban spiritual landscape and the defenders of its peoples. CoG managed to weather the storm rather well, though they still had some stinkers, and surprise surprise, they don't get the capacity to deep six weapons and keep them from working. And, in spite of how very badly the game wants us to imagine otherwise, the Black Furies are quite clearly still invested in Greek myth, and with Gorgon, the Greek myth feminine. I just have might doubts that the writers can pull off clever subversions like &quot;actually, the Greek heroes were terrible&quot;, so who knows where that's going to go as time passes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-11-2024, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T05:06:48-07:00","id":1543579,"title":"","content":"The tribe gifts are seriously where you can see how much they struggled to have so many tribes to suddenly translate gifts from Legacy WtA to a more Forsaken style. And the gifts were meaningless enough that there wasn't even much effort to invent new names for them that weren't cultural.<br /> <br /> Yet they made an effort to make new names for the CoF gifts, because they were a clear focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T11:40:29-07:00","id":1543589,"title":"","content":"Specifically 1e Forsaken style. 2e had facets and different functions by Renown for one Gift, I think. One wonders why they went with 1e.<br /> <br /> Normally, the next three tribes went Fianna - Get of Fenris - Glass Walkers. Feels kind of weird that we're going straight into...<br /> <br /> Galestalkers<br /> <br /> (Younger Brother, except not.)<br /> <br /> Beginner Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Camouflage </div> </div> </div>Told you. Mark that as another stealth Gift that requires HONOR!, though unlike some others, you can spend resources to extend it to your entire pack. Given that you have to stand still, I'm surprised that they didn't also make your cross your arms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lacerating Wind </div> </div> </div>Justin Achilli was obsessing over skipping straight to this over the &quot;fart wind&quot; Gift in one blog post. It gives a group of enemies a penalty or acts as a ranged Falling Touch against one.<br /> <br /> Not Younger Brother also learns Ensnare Spirit.<br /> <br /> Intermediate Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chill Cloak </div> </div> </div>And yet another Gift that improves concealment with HONOR!, with a side of suggesting that some people may not actually know how endothermy and ecothermy work (certainly not the latter, given the spirits identified as teaching the Gift).<br /> <br /> All the other Gifts are repeats - Call the Ridden, Pulse of the Prey, and Wind Claws.<br /> <br /> Elder Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blood of the Wastes </div> </div> </div>Makes life in harsh climates easier based on your HONOR!, as a passive, permanent effect for every form. Also assists in foraging. I guess it's more versatile than Blood of the North, but there was a reason that the survival-assistance Gift wasn't, you know, this far down, and I don't think it's actually difficult to comprehend why.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Claws of Frozen Death </div> </div> </div>May or may not count as a claw gift. Only takes effect in Crinos, and causes your target to be less able to defend against further attacks. I'd ask why this is here and not earlier, but I think I know why.<br /> <br /> Also Rans: Oathbreaker's Bane<br /> <br /> Ghost Council<br /> <br /> (Elder Brother, except not. It's been... reimagined.)<br /> <br /> Beginner Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Augur </div> </div> </div>Scrying under a strange choice for a new name, as you can remote view anything by a reflective surface, such as water. Even a single drop of water, apparently on the other side of the world, though the prior version didn't restrict range, either... which was why it was Rank 3. That's one hell of a swing on range and power for a chargen-available Gift. Truly, this is just as much all over the place as the W:tA of old, so if they were going for a smoother power curve, they botched the roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blackout </div> </div> </div>Instead of Shroud and its ability to simply just make a ten foot cube darken magically, this snuffs out a limited number of light sources. I suppose it can be used to technically turn off electronics by a technicality if they're hooked up to a light or a screen, but if you had a 1000 cubic foot volume go dark, that would have also done it and then some, providing an escape route or avenue for creeping. This seems to be made low-key to play by some kind of &quot;Masquerade&quot; style that W:tA doesn't bother with and prefers to make people sweat through because it's one of the two tenets of the Litany that everyone took seriously. But of course, there's no Litany anymore, effectively.<br /> <br /> Also includes the previously-detailed Sense Danger. Seems like they've got one less Gift here than some others, but Augur is pretty boss, all things considered.<br /> <br /> Intermediate Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Serpent's Coil </div> </div> </div>This is basically turning Coils of the Serpent into mist-based Obtenebration, since while it couldn't inflict damage from grappling prior to W5, it can now. Given how Blackout works, it doesn't surprise me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hands of the Earth </div> </div> </div>Not sure why this got placed here and not as an elder level Gift, as it was an upper mid-ranked Gift in prior editions. It's still fairly effective telekinesis, and even stacks up well against V5's telekinesis, amazingly (this tracks; it had twice the lifting weight as five dots of Movement of the Mind through most of the two games' history).<br /> <br /> Mindspeak is also available.<br /> <br /> Elder Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shrouded Aspect </div> </div> </div>Invisibility under a different name. Lasts for a pathetically short period of time, especially since it got bumped from mid-rank to something only elders get, but such is the trend.<br /> <br /> Dreamwalk, Take the True Form, and Thieving Talons of the Magpie are also available.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers<br /> <br /> Beginner Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Skinbind </div> </div> </div>You can store an object as a magic tattoo. So... why do the Glass Walkers have it, and how did it even get past a developer sweep when the developer for some reason thought that ending up nude after turning into another form is somehow an important horror scene?<br /> <br /> That's your only new Gift, your other choices are Animal Magnetism, Gaia's Candor, and Spider's Song, so here's an important question - how is it that Garou are bad at social interaction, again? GWs seem like they can play anyone like a fiddle just at chargen, or maybe with some Renown boosts.<br /> <br /> Intermediate Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Energize </div> </div> </div>One to beam up. You can power and maintain objects that require electricity on Rage, possibly also requiring a paired Trait roll if it's broken. Local Garou too angry to stop for gas!<br /> <br /> Your other choices are Grasp From Beyond and... Snarl of Challenge? The hell? That's almost as weird as Furies getting Halt the Coward's Flight.<br /> <br /> Elder Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Control Machine </div> </div> </div>For some reason, they couldn't be bothered to divide this between an easy &quot;mechanical objects only&quot; Gift and a harder &quot;Electronics now, too&quot; version. Unlike living things, you can't endanger the objects, and also gets more difficult if you go against the &quot;purpose&quot; of the device, like unlatching a lock. The fuck? It opens and closes. I'd have placed the difficulty as trying to get it to close on someone instead, if I were doing that, but I'm still hung up on &quot;animals will die for you, machines will tell you to go fuck yourself&quot;. I guess I know where the writers' sympathies lie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doppelganger </div> </div> </div>Has an umlaut that I didn't type. Quite frankly, it doesn't deserve it, because it lacks the endurance and effectiveness of the legacy version, but then again, it is a W5 &quot;elder&quot; Gift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Recover Memory </div> </div> </div>It means from a computer data storage device, primarily, though it can also be used on books and other written material. Which raises another question - how is it that they don't know way more archeology than anyone else? If any civilization wrote down anything, it's fair game. You also need other Abilities to understand what you can feel out, though, so it's actually easier to use it on hardcopy texts than on electronic data, as the later requires a Whatever + Technology roll.<br /> <br /> Three tribes that had some of the most interesting tricks in previous material, and what we get is frequently &quot;adjusted&quot; with the expertise of ham hands. Once again, there's also no consistency in power levels or effectiveness to be found. Simple tricks from prior editions (Control Simple Machine) are changed into brutal challenges for no fucking reason at all, the Galestalkers have some random inclusions that, much as Bugerkrieg noted, make them a lot like Forsaken, but with the touch that it's bad because they're erasing inclusion with the approach toward tribes, and the Ghost Council are turning into the Luposombra. I'd really love it if Vampire didn't take over every spread of culture, but given that they took all of the cultures out of W5, I suppose the Vampire stans in charge just defaulted to what they knew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-11-2024, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T14:19:16-07:00","id":1543636,"title":"","content":"For whatever reason, my method for editing things caught the spam filter yesterday. At any rate, we're getting back into the genesis of this thread, with the...<br /> <br /> <s>Fianna</s>Hart Wardens<br /> <br /> (Yeah, we can see through the paint. It started flaking immediately with the Gift section.)<br /> <br /> Beginner Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sacred Boundary </div> </div> </div>You can draw a line in the sand. It doesn't stop anyone, but you'll know if someone crosses it. Also, it has to be drawn with...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (...sacred water from a caern, blood, or their own urine) </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of off-color uses of Spew, a Mokole Gift. At any rate, you can only have one at a time, and it has to be a circle or placed like a tripwire between two objects. It also only lasts for a day or a night, so you'll have to bleed yourself a lot (or do things the wolf way) if you don't have access to a caern. The area also depends on your Glory, which sounds like a setup for a joke.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blessed Brew </div> </div> </div>I know I already touched on that, but... yeah, snrk, some impressive reimagining this is. &quot;Fianna is just a word&quot; indeed. A word that indicates how this wasn't originally written as a reboot, reimagining, or anything but straight up continuity.<br /> <br /> At any rate, this is like the photo negative of vampires trying to get you to drink their blood, as this allows you to ward off mental influence. Only usable once per get together for a game, but it works for an entire bottle.<br /> <br /> Also Rans From the Auspices: Crow's Laughter<br /> <br /> Intermediate Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Territorial Dominance </div> </div> </div>You can mark spots on the perimeter of any size territory during the full moon as long as you can reach them. Then you become the Fisher King... for all of a few days. There's a bonus die in it for most rolls, but if anyone dumps trash on it or despoils it, you'll take actual injury, or at least Emotional Damage. The timing and duration sharply limit the effectiveness of this Gift, so I don't see people picking it up if they ever start adding to Gift lists.<br /> <br /> Also Rans From the Auspices: Beast's Fealty, Song of Inspiration<br /> <br /> (You know, when W20 compared the Fianna to bards, I don't think that &quot;caricature of a D&amp;D bard&quot; is quite what they had in mind...)<br /> <br /> Elder Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Balor's Gaze </div> </div> </div>You know, in past editions, this was a rather severe penalty (-5). Here, it's less than half that, and it can only affect one person at a time, except maybe not even then because of the resisted roll. I know it's been something of a running gag for the elder Gifts in W5 to be incredibly underwhelming, but this is getting tiresome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Living Wood </div> </div> </div>...This should have been in the CoG list first. What the hell, W5? I suppose putting in Warp Frenzy would have revealed that Crinos wasn't really the true end-all, be-all of ripping and tearing (and I think that vampire fans run screaming at the prospect of Gift of the Spriggan actually still existing), but it's fairly obvious that the HWs were Fianna first, so they shouldn't have to poach the CoGs.<br /> <br /> Trees that are nearby will grapple enemies, bushes will grapple enemies less well, nothing else matters unless the ST is feeling generous. May or may not also be used to grow plants; it's rather non-committal to the idea.<br /> <br /> Also Rans From the Auspices: Kiss of Helios, Living Ward<br /> <br /> Red Talons<br /> <br /> Beginner Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hidden Killer </div> </div> </div>Previously, this made werewolf-made wounds look like knives and gunshots to make it look like some kind of illicit deal gone wrong, a mugging, etc. Now it completely eliminates signs of injury, so that corpses look like mysteriously exsanguinated bodies. The text specifically highlights that they resemble the victims of someone who really wanted to get that last Hunger Die ticked off, so they're either going for Red Talons being the most ardent enemies of vampires like in 1e's text for them, or they just wanted to make them act like the Sabbat. I'd say that the tack the writing takes leans toward the latter, but the book is kind of back and forth about Garou interacting with vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Render Down </div> </div> </div>Technically improved in one respect from its last appearance in W20, as it allows you to turn an entire car into a pile of glass, metal, and oil. Not so improved for requiring minutes to work or relying on HONOR!<br /> <br /> Also Rans: Razor Claws (Red Talons are the new Fenrir!), Song of Rage (urgh)<br /> <br /> Intermediate Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gaia's Embrace </div> </div> </div>Would not have pinned gravity control as a Red Talon thing. This penalizes ranged weapon use and causes flying characters to regret flying, as they experience a little slice of the BattleTech in-universe instructional film for aerospace pilots, &quot;Deconstructive Lithobraking: When the Ground Is Not Your Friend&quot;. Of course, if you were flying at the altitude level in BT where you could get this Gift used on you, you were already likely to crash, anyway. Has about a three hex radius, in BT board game terms. Also applies Honor as a straight penalty to ranged attacked (presumably only with projectiles and not energy beams, but since the Technocracy is unlikely to show up, ever, in 5e WoD, we may never know). VTOLs are also likely to crash, but that's VTOLs for you. That armor limit of only two on the rotor is a killer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Quicksand </div> </div> </div>If your enemy is on soil, you can make them reenact the scene from The Neverending Story that makes everyone bawl. It's only a -2 penalty (ofc) but it also caps movement at walking speed.<br /> <br /> Also Rans: Fangs of Judgment<br /> <br /> Elder Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shield of the Wyld </div> </div> </div>AKA Shield of Gaia, except not. At any rate, this is limited to reducing a limited amount of damage against constructed weapons that aren't made of silver or those that have a spirit in them. For reference, the original was a legendary Gift that gave the one learning it a choice about which form of technology they could be permanently unaffected by, with the only limit being that you couldn't choose nukes. And from then on, you couldn't be shot if you chose guns, couldn't be recorded or photographed if you chose cameras, etc. But you won't be getting that, because this is W5.<br /> <br /> Also Rans: Feral Regression, The Thousand Forms<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fatal Flaw </div> </div> </div>You learn what ways someone will take agg. This can be used to soft-spot vampires, because &quot;throw them out into the sun&quot; is probably a good indication of that, even if not infallible. Can also give a damage bonus, if you've done your research. Pretty comparable, since the old version could add on one die of damage, but then gave somewhat more abstract definitions of flaws, like insecurities or vulnerabilities, as it was based on the Empathy Ability and all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Icy Chill of Despair </div> </div> </div>Now, the previous version of this was one par with Majesty, the Presence 5 power. This one... is not, and that's kind of a travesty. It's just a de-buff to spending or regaining WP.<br /> <br /> Also Rans: Shadow Sense<br /> <br /> Intermediate Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dire Distraction </div> </div> </div>The activation roll for this Gift is odd in that it is a &quot;guess who?&quot; for the origin of the effect. Why one curses with Glory, though, I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> The rest of this level for the Lords is also-rans. I'm getting tired of listing them, so blurry, starey, and scary will have to do.<br /> <br /> Elder Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thunderclap </div> </div> </div>This one has an odd duration that suggests it knocks people to the ground for an entire scene, but that couldn't be correct. May also inflict a penalty against others. I'm not sure why this is here, and yet, there is that recurring issue with the elder gifts...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Under the Gun </div> </div> </div>Mostly comparable to the old version, which is damning with faint praise, on account of how that was a mid-ranked Gift and not, say, the ability to spawn shadow clones or supernatural compulsion. Basically, the only Gift in this tier that fits is the one that lets them be Lelouch... kind of.<br /> <br /> The reduced scale of these is getting grating, especially since a lot more Disciplines from V5 managed to avoid getting nerfed at all, and inherent powers like blood bonding or boosting Attributes were left more or less untouched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T03:52:23-07:00","id":1543673,"title":"","content":"One has to wonder if this nerfing is intentional in case of crossover, or is it to prevent players from ACTUALLY trying fix things?<br /> <br /> Or, most damning, is it because the people translating the gifts from Legacy's system just rushed and copied mechanics from similar gifts in Forsaken?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T05:08:04-07:00","id":1543675,"title":"","content":"I think in W5 you don't really pick Gifts and Rites based on character-choices. Due to the combination of how weak a lot of Gifts are and how punishing the system can be, the best way to approach this is to concentrate on the resource-management of your Rage and make sure you always go into combat with high Rage and keep it at a low level when you're doing more social/sneaky stuff. And for that reason, the first category of Gifts/Rites you should focus on are the ones that let are the ones that let you manage your Rage-score. The next-best ones are the ones that are about dealing with the Umbra (letting you peek into it, Spirit-stuff). And the third one are all the Gift that give you a die-bonus based on your Renown-rating when you do certain things.<br /> <br /> The rest you can take it or leave it, I think. Especially because if you don't manage your Rage properly and you end up losing the wolf, you can't use Gifts or Rites. And if for whatever reason, you end up in a situation where you enter Frenzy, you can't use Gifts either. So in that sense, the game almost begs players to focus on &quot;gaming the systems&quot; by focusing on stuff like Song of Rage or the Rite of Rage. If you don't do that, the system will kick your butt and then you won't be able to use the Gifts and Rites you picked instead anyway.<br /> <br /> And once you're in combat, you're better off just throwing the Crinos Form at whatever obstacle the ST has put in front of you. You're keeping Rage in reserve for Regeneration and hoping you can trigger Brutal Outcomes on your rolls in combat. And you also need a reserve of WP, so that you don't enter Frenzy in your Crinos-Form. This system does not reward characters for trying to get clever with Gifts. And ST are in a bit of a pickle here as well. If they're more lenient with the strength of the enemies to allow players to spend Rage/WP on using Gifts, then the person who's using the Crinos Form as a blunt instrument just smashes the enemy into pieces with Brutal Outcomes and the Crinos Form long before the PC who's trying to employ some strategy using Gifts does anything. If ST creates opponents that can go toe-to-toe with a high Rage Crinos Form, then they will beat the shit out of any PC that's spending Rage on using Gifts rather than reserving it for Regeneration or a lack of WP leads to Frenzy when they're in their Crinos Form and after that, they're forced into playing &quot;Crinos Form as a blunt instrument&quot; anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T08:09:49-07:00","id":1543679,"title":"","content":"And yet they say the STs should make sure the players don't strategize with their Rage XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T09:44:10-07:00","id":1543686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1543679#post1543679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet they say the STs should make sure the players don't strategize with their Rage XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yeah, that sidebar on pg 132... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It even says: &quot;Likewise, a Storyteller should be mindful of players attempting to game the system by using Gifts or other abilities for the sake of dumping Rage.&quot; But, look, what else does the Gift Song of Serenity and Rite of Tranquility do? The same way Rite of Rage is transparently just a tool to increase Rage, those are tools to decrease Rage. And Rite of the Wolf Reborn is just a tool to reverse &quot;losing the wolf&quot; without having to wait for a character to howl at the moon.<br /> <br /> And I don't really see the appeal in playing W5 in a way where the ST isn't very liberal and forgiving in how PCs can gain Rage. Because a scarcity leads to one of two things: Either you're gonna invest in those abilities that rules-as-written just let you increase/decrease your Rage or you're running a game of WtA where shifting, using Gifts and fighting rarely happens. The latter isn't even about the torment of being a werewolf. If anything it's about the PC being wary of using their werewolf-powers because they're constantly so close to losing the wolf. In that scenario, it's all about the PC having werewolf-powers but being unable to access them. That would be the conflict. Not that being a Garou with Rage is a cursed existence.<br /> <br /> This also reminds me of this bit on pg 135 where the corebook is concerned about players shifting too often: &quot;Note that too-frequent (or frivolous\u2026) shifting takes a terrible toll on body and mind. Should a character shift back and forth multiple times in a short time span, such as by seeking simply to shed Rage, the Storyteller may realize such massive bodily stress by inflicting appropriate levels of Aggravated damage to Health and/or Willpower. (Let the player know before you do so, the better to inform their decision-making.)\u200b&quot; The only reason you could be shifting so many times in this game is that if you stay in a supernatural Form you have to take Rage-checks at the start of every scene and at the same time you need to be in a supernatural Form to be able to use most of the Gifts. So, this game is punishing you both for shifting to a supernatural Form and staying in it but also for not being in a supernatural Form. But still, the writers here thought it necessary to add that the ST should consider punishing PCs for shifting too often...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T10:15:28-07:00","id":1543689,"title":"","content":"The developer of the time also said that he got rid of talisman dedication because waking up nude was apparently an essential horror experience* but I see that the rite is still there, so... utter chaos reigns and nothing matters, I guess.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">* And not just an embarrassing Sunday morning.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T10:41:54-07:00","id":1543693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1543686#post1543686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don't really see the appeal in playing W5 in a way where the ST isn't very liberal and forgiving in how PCs can gain Rage. Because a scarcity leads to one of two things: Either you're gonna invest in those abilities that rules-as-written just let you increase/decrease your Rage or you're running a game of WtA where shifting, using Gifts and fighting rarely happens. The latter isn't even about the torment of being a werewolf. If anything it's about the PC being wary of using their werewolf-powers because they're constantly so close to losing the wolf. In that scenario, it's all about the PC having werewolf-powers but being unable to access them. That would be the conflict. Not that being a Garou with Rage is a cursed existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>The cherry on top is that, from what I've seen from the adventures released, the stingy using of Rage, shifting and gifts is not in fact the intended way to play. Most of the adventures have combat against supernatural foes. So one would assume using the powers is encouraged.<br /> <br /> But the core outright punishes you for trying to play the game as intended. Herding the PCs to focus on human stuff just so they don't have to deal with the Rage rigmarole.<br /> <br /> And wolf-born aren't considered, once again XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T13:43:02-07:00","id":1543700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1543693#post1543693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The cherry on top is that, from what I've seen from the adventures released, the stingy using of Rage, shifting and gifts is not in fact the intended way to play. Most of the adventures have combat against supernatural foes. So one would assume using the powers is encouraged.<br /> <br /> But the core outright punishes you for trying to play the game as intended. Herding the PCs to focus on human stuff just so they don't have to deal with the Rage rigmarole.<br /> <br /> And wolf-born aren't considered, once again XD</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Losing the wolf&quot; is the real cherry on top in W5 with all its punishing mechanics. Like take Isle of the Splintered Dreams... In the last act when you're doing the super-important Rite and you're rushing to the caern, when you fail a test you get ambushed by certain members of the bad Garou-Pack. Now imagine you got the player who still hasn't figured out how things work and they somehow manage to lose the wolf. The real final confrontation is supposed to happen, though, when you get to the caern and do the Rite. So what are you supposed to do with a PC that has lost the wolf? But even if you're aware of the consequences... this is a system where you have to think &quot;Can I use this Gift or could the required Rage-check push me to Rage 0?&quot; Rage 1 is also perilous. You do Rage-checks for Regeneration after all. And going into Crinos requires two Rage-checks. Also, consider that this is the official rule for shifting: &quot;If the check causes them to lose their final point of Rage, the shift fails and they lose the wolf, as a Garou needs at least one point of Rage to stay in a supernatural form.&quot; This means you need at least three dots in Rage to be 100% certain that you're gonna shift into your Crinos Form when the player wants to.<br /> <br /> And then you look at all these Gifts that just make you wonder why you would wanna risk doing any Rage-checks or spend WP in this environment for some piddly supernatural power or effect.<br /> <br /> Also you're right... Ha, hadn't thought about it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ... &quot;Losing your wolf&quot; is a bit of a poor choice of words with wolf-born Garou in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T23:41:33-07:00","id":1543737,"title":"","content":"It would be funny if a ST ran Splintered Dreams in a very orthodox way... and ended up with all their players in homid and unable to do the rite.<br /> <br /> This is a great example why shifting didn't require Rage in Legacy AND why the Rage pool was bigger than 5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1543700#post1543700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also you're right... Ha, hadn't thought about it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ... &quot;Losing your wolf&quot; is a bit of a poor choice of words with wolf-born Garou in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the poor sods just get stuck in homid, since the writing implies garou cannot communicate with wolves anymore.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T13:04:15-07:00","id":1543777,"title":"","content":"We have reached an abbreviated end to the Gifts! So I guess I'll also cover the rites as well. There aren't many of them.<br /> <br /> Silent Striders<br /> <br /> Beginner Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fetch Bounty </div> </div> </div>Basically an amalgamation of every Gift that could scrounge something important. Need to find non-poisonous mushrooms in the woods? This can do it. Need a car of a particular make and model? This can do it. It can only find what's there, though; it can't match the foraging capabilities of Exalted Charms. Quite frankly, I'd expect this Gift to suit the Bone Gnawers more, but again, PDX wanted them to be the Dogsferatu, so they were flattened into the Dogsferatu.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Speech of the World </div> </div> </div>The text of this Gift specifies living languages are targets for reading and writing, but the rules section ignores that and allows you to read clay tablets to find out how people were getting screwed by a bronze merchant. Much like the GWs and their penchant for being able to lift information from ancient sources, this is something that should give the Garou the capacity to know massive amounts of ancient information even in light of W5's bias against oral history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whispered Passaged </div> </div> </div>Gnawing off your leg (quiet, quiet)<br /> Limping to the cottage (quiet, quiet)<br /> Now you're on the doorstep<br /> Sitting inside<br /> Shia LeBeouf!<br /> <br /> Completely mutes the character, mostly mutes everything else around them, in a classic case of &quot;quiet... too quiet...&quot;.<br /> <br /> Intermediate Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Burrow </div> </div> </div>This was a Crinos-born Gift in legacy, as they tended to have the run of various assorted &quot;animal theme powers&quot; other than maybe one Gift that provided venom being for lupus. Here, it's more or less on par with its old self, it's just that it's kind of weird it shows up in the Silent Strider list. They can still make use of it in theme (The Great Escape time!), but the collapse of splats does that. Also, instead of being free, you have to make a Rage check.<br /> <br /> Other picks are soapy and spirit safety.<br /> <br /> <br /> Elder Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Golden Path </div> </div> </div>Slight buff to notice dangers both direct (explosives) and abstract (cameras). Useful, but again, this Elder-tier Gift is not exactly wowing me.<br /> <br /> Other picks for this tier are defiant, zwee fighting, and married to duty.<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs<br /> <br /> Beginner Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pack Instinct </div> </div> </div>Basically lets the Fang operate with the information that you would normally have if you were playing a video game directing your fellow Garou. Would have been useful and in-theme for Ahrouns, but forget it Jake, it's W5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Silver Compact </div> </div> </div>Protects you from being attacked or damaged by spirits and whatever they might possess.<br /> <br /> Also gets: howly<br /> <br /> Intermediate Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blood of the Pack </div> </div> </div>A limited number of times per scene, you can have the people who aren't in danger of losing the wolf make Rage checks for the ones who are. A band-aid on an amputation, quite frankly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unity of the Pack </div> </div> </div>You can also spend WP for each other!... except for the &quot;also&quot;, because it's not compatible with the above.<br /> <br /> Also gets: gathery<br /> <br /> Elder Gifts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Luna's Avenger </div> </div> </div>Amongst the travesties of the Gift list, this is by far the most insulting. It has nothing to do with turning into a Crinos of living silver, and everything to do with getting a buff to attack and defense for every packmate that's injured or near death, which is limited by your HONOR!<br /> <br /> I'll see you in hell, W5. Also, the Fangs get some other shit here, too... spirit boss, silver-away, silver yes.<br /> <br /> Rites<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of Abjuration </div> </div> </div>The association with a D&amp;D spell school makes me cringe, no matter how appropriate it is. Kicks spirits out of everything around... including your Talismans (aka fetishes). Brutal failures make the attempt go sideways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of Rage </div> </div> </div>Back in my day, if a ritual duel went bad, someone died, and didn't just take a level of superficial or something. Gets you more Rage, where more is &quot;one point, maybe two&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of Tranquility </div> </div> </div>Sets Rage to 1, with the risk of Emotional Damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of Contrition </div> </div> </div>Specifically targets chagrin (Renown dysfunction when you act against its ideals) and spirits that are angry at you, as opposed to an attempt at starting to generally ask for forgiveness in Garou society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of the Forgetful Record </div> </div> </div>You would be forgiven for thinking that this is why there's pretty much no history to W5's Garou. It actually messes up evidence that people have collected about the participants of the rite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of the Living Caern </div> </div> </div>It's the Moot Rite, but since Garou can only have their own human culture or a vampire clan's culture, we apparently can't just call it that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of Shadow Passage </div> </div> </div>And speaking of travesties, not being successful at crossing the Gauntlet means that you still cross, with none of the potential complications for adventure. Also it relies on how well you've read up on your Occult, and not an innate connection to the spirit world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of Dedication </div> </div> </div>Couldn't be called talisman dedication because talisman is the new word for fetish. But, it's still there, now limited by time and... being washed. Some triatic explanation is roped in, because apparently the directive is to just ignore Gaia being at the mid-point of the three.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of Kinseeking </div> </div> </div>It's not kin-fetch, even as unreliable as kin-fetches sometimes are. If the rite goes well you get... a slight bonus on attempts to track or generally locate not yet changed Garou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of Spirit Summoning </div> </div> </div>PDX, what else are the Garou going to summon? Pretty much as you'd expect it, except that the writing assumes a higher likelihood that the spirit doesn't like you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of Binding </div> </div> </div>Can only stuff a spirit into physical object or living being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of Shame </div> </div> </div>Intensifies chagrin. That's it. That's how it works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of Patronage </div> </div> </div>Lets your pack use another tribe's Patron benefit in addition to your own tribe's, or you double up on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of Celebration </div> </div> </div>Regains wp. Can only be used once per story, and only if you managed to succeed at something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of Caern Building </div> </div> </div>Also used to repair or improve the rating of a caern. Hope you're a professional in construction, because you'll need it for the roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of the Wolf Reborn </div> </div> </div>Gives Garou back the wolf. Can go sideways in some bad ways, but it's also not restricted in how often in can be used... assuming that you have a pack, and the pack has enough Rage between them to make it work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of the Whispering Field </div> </div> </div>What was wrong with the name &quot;The Badger's Burrow&quot;, exactly? Anyway, this does the same thing, letting you know when there are trespassers about. Except that it only provides a small bonus to this, and can go sideways, since W5 is RAGERAGERAGERAGE without the slightest hint of Essence or Gnosis to be found.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite of the Shrouded Glen </div> </div> </div>Requires weaving together vines or anything else long, thin, and flexible to accomplish a fairly minor version of Enchant the Forest (the rite it shares a name with in legacy actually works to conceal an area in the Umbra proper, not the area around the caern).<br /> <br /> There were also some &quot;Social Rites&quot; listed that don't have rules for them: Rite of Passage, Satire Rite, Rite of Accomplishment, Gathering for the Departed, and Rite of the Winter Wolf.<br /> <br /> At any rate, the section in the book also covers Talismans. Talens still exist, incidentally. They're referred to as temporary talismans, and include... single use klaives. I shit you not. Also the klaive apparently doesn't account for a potential war-spirit in it, so it only does silver damage, not general agg. That, of course raises the important question of WHHHHHYYYYYYY?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T01:49:55-07:00","id":1543848,"title":"","content":"The Rites are also a bit of a mess. First off, the distinction between &quot;Common Rites&quot; and &quot;Social Rites&quot; doesn't make sense. The only way it is a distinction is that the writers bothered to write rules for the first category and not the second. Because what else are Rite of Shame, Rite of Contrition and Rite of Celebration if not &quot;Social Rites&quot;?<br /> <br /> But those two also bring up an element in W5 I hate and it's &quot;chagrin&quot;. Rather than hashing out Renown gains and losses at Moots or some other kind of social gathering, the way Renown is handled in W5 is that a particular Renown-track can be put &quot;in chagrin&quot; (ie it counts as one dot less). And how does that happen?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;When a Garou acts in overt opposition to a Renown virtue\u2019s creed, and in an especially noteworthy way, the Storyteller may declare that character to be in chagrin. Mark that Renown type on the character sheet as subject to chagrin.&quot; </div> </div> </div>So the way the W5 corebook envisions this is that a PC does something and if it breaks the tenets of that particular Renown, that Renown type is put &quot;in chagrin&quot;. But it's all up to the ST. That puts a huge burden on the ST for how to regulate this and on the player for having to figure out what the exact rules of Renown are. The way I handled it wasn't exactly like it's described in the corebook because I had a situation where one PC got into a fight with the guards as two of them were sneaking into a warehouse. And the second one wanted to move on and leave the other one behind. So I told that player I would put his Honor in chagrin if he were to leave his packmate behind when he's in trouble. And so what we agreed upon was what he did instead is that he announced himself to the guards, the first player who got in trouble told the second one that he could handle this alone and he should move on.<br /> <br /> And removing chagrin is the same thing. The book wants you to talk to the ST and the ST then tells you how you can get out of chagrin. Again, it's all on the ST to make this work.<br /> <br /> This chagrin-&quot;system&quot; also only gets even more confounding when you add the Silver Fangs Ban to it: &quot;If a Silver Fang takes an action that causes them to risk chagrin or losing Renown, they may recover only a single Willpower at the start of the next session, instead of their Composure or Resolve rating.\u200b&quot; (I could almost believe that this is another one of those cases where this was copy-pasted from the draft of the Hunters Entertainment version and that's why this makes little sense in the context of the actual chagrin rules in this book. Because there's no &quot;risking chagrin&quot; in the way it's outlined.)<br /> <br /> If you were to do it as described, I guess the players are supposed to read the mind of the ST to know what actions would put them in chagrin and which ones wouldn't and the ST is supposed to read the minds of any Silver Fang player so that whenever these PCs come even close to doing something that would put their Renown in chagrin, the ST can trigger the Ban.<br /> <br /> And then you get to the Rites which are connected to this...<ul><li>Rite of Shame makes chagrin worse. The problem is that the declaration of this Renown-violation wasn't made by anyone within the setting but rather by the ST. If a PC does something that puts them in chagrin but nobody knows that they did this thing, did the Renown-violation really happen?</li> <li>Rite of Contrition needlessly turns the &quot;removing chagrin&quot;-process into a mechanic. Especially because as a Rite where of course Rage-dice are now getting involved, you get this: &quot;A Brutal outcome causes a failure and means that additional offense was caused, and further penance must be made before the Rite can be tried again. (The nature of this penance depends on the grievance and the offended parties, and is up to the Storyteller.)\u200b&quot; You're <i>already </i>in the process of doing penance in a way that is up to the ST! How does it make sense to add this caveat of &quot;But if you have a Brutal Outcome in this Rite that's all about doing penance, you have to do penance <i>again</i>!&quot;...?</li> <li>Rite of Celebration in this system feels completely neutered. Renown are just dots you buy to get better at doing Gifts and hopefully there's a narrative justification. So, it's just a way to heal WP-damage... except the restriction is weird: &quot;This Rite can be performed only after the pack has achieved a victory. It can be attempted, only once\u200b per story, to allow the pack to restore Willpower above and beyond the norm.\u200b&quot; With that restriction in mind, doing the Rite after the victory at the end makes sense - except why would you need WP-healing at the end of the story...? But doing this &quot;once per story&quot;-celebration in the middle of the story after a partial victory also feels weird.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T21:11:31-07:00","id":1544257,"title":"","content":"Okay, so back to chapter 2. How much worse can it get?<br /> <br /> Well, the windup in the beginning paragraph wants the Garou to be the only, or perhaps primary, society in which violent conflict happens. This is a bit of the wrong place to start, because states of humans only become states because of their monopoly on violence, and they were really violent until rather recently.<br /> <br /> Of course, it also dwells on the unreliability of oral history... because it made the Garou no longer write things down, apparently? Maybe it was those overdone glyphs we see in the splat definition section that made them quit literacy in their own ideograms. There's no real excuse for axing the glyph system of writing, either; even if they can't use it in Crinos because someone wanted to turn it into a complete Rage-bomb with no subtlety or other uses, Razor Claws could allow any form to write in it... which would awkwardly make a number of other splats the premiere scribes of history. Like most concepts that stem from the implications of powers, however, W5 is absolutely uninterested in exploration of the concept, and just wants to cram its themes and moods down the reader's throat.<br /> <br /> We're then told about the origins of Garou, and Fera, if they keep that term. There's a claim that they're meant to keep the Triat in balance, and so good so far, but then it veers into keeping spirit and material worlds in balance, which... no, W5 writers! That's Forsaken's thing! The proper balance of W:tA is to restore spirit and the material to being one united whole! This is where trying to mash together W:tF and W:tA works out the worst. The existence of the Fera is kept way too vague for beings that you're going to be bumping into a lot without much untamed wilderness to share, and we get back to the old standard of W:tA where the Garou declare themselves to be more important than the other changers... probably?<br /> <br /> We get some angry margin notes where someone sticks up for not calling humans &quot;the Weaver's children&quot;. It's gonna be real awkward for that character if gorgons opt not to possess humans again in this edition. Much F bomb, so vibing.<br /> <br /> The narrative of the Impergium wants to make it sound like all Garou were all terrible violence for millennia and there was no one that thought to use compassion or reason for however long W5 wants it to have lasted. There's also a sidebar that presents the discovery and use of silver like it was the Inquisition against the Kindred or something, when it's traditionally been a case of &quot;okay, you have some reasonably pure silver weapons. Now you have a chance in hell, maybe.&quot; It conveniently ignores in said sidebar that the Delirium was a thing that would have been developing and making it really hard for &quot;hunters&quot; to stand up to Crinos werewolves. But for that matter, why would the Garou be carrying out the Impergium in Crinos? The form where they end up almost always losing the wolf after going on a murder bender?<br /> <br /> The origin of the Garou Nation is in place as usual, but without the link of kinfolk, which makes it kind of wobbly. The Garou are presented as having a love of dominance alone, instead of being parts of extended families that drag each other into obligations. The date where the White Howlers fell is also really hazy, as without their isolation in what would become Scotland, how being ushered into the Spiral Labyrinth one and all would shake out is not a detail that the text feels like sharing or dwelling on.<br /> <br /> ...They kept the &quot;mysterious disappearance&quot; of Roanoke. I can't even.<br /> <br /> Thousands of years of history get glossed over really, really quickly, here. It isn't just the last few decades that don't make sense or don't have a cogent progression of events. Though, really, that was probably intentional.<br /> <br /> Luna finally gets mentioned when it's time to talk about auspices. Which are no longer capitalized, ever. Tribes are given a terrible introduction, with the CoGs being described like Stargazers, Bone Gnawers being nailed down as the Dogsferatu, and Black Furies get someone squatting on their cause by calling what they rage against &quot;perceived injustice&quot;. The Hart Wardens and Galestalkers are borderline non-tribes. The Ghost Council is supposed to take on &quot;unconventional methods&quot; of getting the job done, but in a game where you won't even be straight up about what convention is, this has no meaning at all. The Shadow Lords are the new Get of Fenris, and none of this has any seeming weight at all.<br /> <br /> The BSDs are first introduced as hating Gaia and wanting to defile what remains of her. Sounds like really nice guys, there! Just the kind you would want to try and fix, unlike the Fenrir or Stargazers!<br /> <br /> There's a quote from Mari Cabrah. It's empty of any characterization she had prior to W5.<br /> <br /> Also, there's a bunch of stuff shotgunned about what's behind who becomes Garou and who doesn't that tries to make a giant mystery out of it when it was perfect fine to just say that Gaia did it. I can, however, definitively and without any doubt say this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it genetic? </div> </div> </div>No. That shouldn't have even been in the running. Proteins can't make you half spirit.<br /> <br /> Some Glass Walker idly considers that becoming Garou might be a punishment reincarnation and that everyone who is Garou was terrible in a past life. I think that's just code for what the editor of the WoD5 thinks of W:tA players from past editions, rephrased, honestly.<br /> <br /> I'm calling it there, for now. The &quot;balance spirit and the material&quot; thing from back up there is really grinding my gears; it's such an elementary difference between Forsaken and Apocalypse that you cannot just throw it in and hope to keep the game intact. But, as with everything else, keeping anything was obviously not on the docket, which is odd. They bought it, and now they're not going to use as much of it as possible? Forsaken doesn't line up with what people saw from Bloodlines 1, bruh. You're just going to make everyone awfully confused with the changes while you seemingly go out of your way to aggravated everyone who made the game's continued existence possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T02:43:17-07:00","id":1544269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ghost Council is supposed to take on &quot;unconventional methods&quot; of getting the job done, but in a game where you won't even be straight up about what convention is, this has no meaning at all. </div> </div> </div>The way the Tribe is presented in W5, it's an outright evil Tribe. I saw the writer of the Book of Hungry Names game talk about how he thinks their shtick is &quot;using the Wyrm's tools against the Wyrm&quot;. And then of course in Scent of Decay, the last adventure is about how the Horned Serpent Patron Spirit encouraged a Garou Pack to let the Wyrm run rampant in a small town as a way to &quot;study the Wyrm&quot;.<br /> <br /> This one and the Red Talons with their Plague Dog character-concept, I have a hard time seeing what's the difference between those two Tribes and BSD in W5. Especially because Shattered Nation describes how Black Spiral Dancers can sometimes be your allies in the fight against Pentex and how they still care a lot about their White Howler legacy. Honestly, the BSD in W5 sound more reasonable than the descriptions they have for the Ghost Council or Red Talons in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T03:15:16-07:00","id":1544270,"title":"","content":"In regards to them using Forsaken stuff, a Ropecon panel stated that the writers don't treat WtA and WtF as separate games with separate settings. They treat CofD as an AU of WoD they can take stuff from. Hence the spirit vs physical balance thing.<br /> <br /> But as you can see, not even THAT is really focused on. There is no cohesion to be found, just disparate ideas floating in the aether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T09:34:02-07:00","id":1544294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544269#post1544269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way the Tribe is presented in W5, it's an outright evil Tribe. I saw the writer of the Book of Hungry Names game talk about how he thinks their shtick is &quot;using the Wyrm's tools against the Wyrm&quot;. And then of course in Scent of Decay, the last adventure is about how the Horned Serpent Patron Spirit encouraged a Garou Pack to let the Wyrm run rampant in a small town as a way to &quot;study the Wyrm&quot;.<br /> <br /> This one and the Red Talons with their Plague Dog character-concept, I have a hard time seeing what's the difference between those two Tribes and BSD in W5. Especially because Shattered Nation describes how Black Spiral Dancers can sometimes be your allies in the fight against Pentex and how they still care a lot about their White Howler legacy. Honestly, the BSD in W5 sound more reasonable than the descriptions they have for the Ghost Council or Red Talons in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That almost sounds like the BSDs have some idea of what their legacy is. I doubt that they do, though, because this is W5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to them using Forsaken stuff, a Ropecon panel stated that the writers don't treat WtA and WtF as separate games with separate settings. They treat CofD as an AU of WoD they can take stuff from. Hence the spirit vs physical balance thing.<br /> <br /> But as you can see, not even THAT is really focused on. There is no cohesion to be found, just disparate ideas floating in the aether.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't Forsaken or Apocalypse anymore; it's Werewolf: the Promethean!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T09:48:10-07:00","id":1544296,"title":"","content":"I also love how BSDs, the ones the core says still look utterly monstrous thanks to the Wyrm, are treated as more viable allies than CoF who are on the same goddamn side as the PCs. /s","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T10:31:11-07:00","id":1544300,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's weird, isn't it? The W5 version of BSD is very aware of and interested in its White Howler legacy but according to Shattered Nation the 80s and 90s are considered &quot;ancient history&quot; by the good Garou...<br /> <br /> I could stomach a lot of W5's changes if it weren't for the bad worldbuilding underpinning it. Nearly everything feels like it got caught up in the contradiction of trying to produce a new edition of WtA and having a deep resentment for WtA as a franchise. The main-phrase for W5 is &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot; but while there are changes - none of them are effective. The changes range from incoherent, half-assed to simply mean-spirited. It's worse for H5 but both the released W5 corebook and H5 corebook are just an anchor around these gamelines' necks. Neither the H5 nor the W5 corebooks give you worldbuilding you want to expand, these books offer worldbuilding you want to <i>reject</i>. Both these corebooks offer such stringent limitations on what the game is supposed to be while offering little to no support for even doing the specific thing they're aiming for.<br /> <br /> Just think of this: In the way the W5 corebook describes its setting, every adventure put on a page by Renegade or in the corebook is a meaningless sideshow. There's the whole idea of W5 decrying Garou as bad and incompetent but then every single adventure afterward is all about how the good thing the PC-Garou-Pack should do is to be a bunch of traditionalists. &quot;Maintain the status quo.&quot; is the core-message of all the material released thus far. In other words &quot;The bad guys are bad, so you have to fight them - but at least be polite about it. There's such a thing as &quot;going too far&quot;, you know.&quot;. And the name for that is Hauglosk. &quot;You think you can change things for the better by being proactive? Sounds like you're suffering from Hauglosk.&quot; No, what W5 envisions you should do is have the players take over a caern and just sit there, protecting it and deal in street-level-adventures that concern that caern. Does it matter that it's the so-called Age of Apocalypse and the world is closer to the Apocalypse than ever...? Nah... don't worry about it. And actually worrying about that and getting angry about that is a sign of Hauglosk - which is bad. And that's why you shouldn't do that.<br /> <br /> These days it doesn't feel like the Garou you're supposed to play in W5 are radicals. They're more like a morality-police. You fight against Fomori because they're &quot;bad people&quot; and you fight against other Garou because they're &quot;bad people&quot;. And what are you fighting for? That everything's fine and hey, if you want to change things, that's okay... they feel bad, though, because the way you're doing it is wrong which is why it needs to get shut down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T15:42:56-07:00","id":1544311,"title":"","content":"Isn't Forsaken pretty much about being a cop? No surprise that trying to stuff massive amounts of it in Apocalypse leads that kind of incongruous messaging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T16:09:50-07:00","id":1544316,"title":"","content":"&quot;Spirit cops&quot; is one of those Internet forums memes that spread around a lot about Forsaken 1e despite being very surface level understanding of the game. Forsaken werewolves are territorial, and that includes maintaining the spiritual and physical sides of their territories. Since the Shadow is more antagonistic in Forsaken than the Umbra is in Apocalypse, many Uratha resort to &quot;maintenance&quot; through force... aka being &quot;spirit cops,&quot; rather than that actually being the point of what Forsaken is about.<br /> <br /> I think it's very telling that W5 reflects far more early surface level Forsaken 1e (aka when Justin was working on Forsaken) than what Forsaken has grown into to help clarify and better actualize its themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T17:00:21-07:00","id":1544321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544316#post1544316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Spirit cops&quot; is one of those Internet forums memes that spread around a lot about Forsaken 1e despite being very surface level understanding of the game. Forsaken werewolves are territorial, and that includes maintaining the spiritual and physical sides of their territories. Since the Shadow is more antagonistic in Forsaken than the Umbra is in Apocalypse, many Uratha resort to &quot;maintenance&quot; through force... aka being &quot;spirit cops,&quot; rather than that actually being the point of what Forsaken is about.<br /> <br /> I think it's very telling that W5 reflects far more early surface level Forsaken 1e (aka when Justin was working on Forsaken) than what Forsaken has grown into to help clarify and better actualize its themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I didn't manage to get into it in spite of a number of books and much time.<br /> <br /> And, again, this is W5. We only get shallow readings of anything, because apparently anything even slightly deeper in the core robs them of the opportunity to place it in another book later on, if they even want to deal with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T17:22:20-07:00","id":1544326,"title":"","content":"W5 is pretty much all surface....you try to go deeper and everything just falls apart. *redacted* was probably the worst possible choice as a Werewolf Developer because he wasn't really interested in depth...in his own words that is up to the players and STs to bring to the world...........even if all the tools to do so have been removed, apparently.<br /> <br /> Actually scratch that....*redacted* is still worse because of his internalised racism and inability to look beyond his own experience of the world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 10-19-2024, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":4},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T18:05:15-07:00","id":1544331,"title":"","content":"Well, if the section on Garou culture and the Litany actually spent time discussing its matter, it would quickly show itself for what it is - a strawman argument. In fact, you can pretty much say that about everything in W5 - it's someone's strawman of W:tA, meant only to fall down and fail to every weak argument made by the text. And, just like a strawman, it has no blood and nothing vital to it.It's a wonder that they could even touch having the Philodox auspice being present, because their entire role in Garou society is to argue about these points - the letter and intent of the law, which is difficult if you get neither presented to you. Are they waiting for some kind of Litany book? One would have imagined that Shattered Nation would have been about that in large part, but it doesn't seem to be the case. It sounds more like The King Albrecht Show, But On Drugs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T01:33:25-07:00","id":1544378,"title":"","content":"The discussion of types of packs neglects to mention an obvious one. Well, a few obvious ones, from when W:tA was about a war. Because while it isn't always the best tool to use, sometimes you've got to go in like a loud team of hooders from Shadowrun - another game that's had issues about &quot;to shoot the suit, or not to shoot the suit...&quot;<br /> <br /> I do believe that, in the end, SR6 has come out on the side of &quot;fuck 'em, shoot!&quot;<br /> <br /> The section Litany mentions that the Garou know it, and that one of the ways that they might is from glyphs etched onto warning stones in the Black Forest. Well, there goes any justification that the text has for ignoring that Garou do, in fact, write down their history. Regrettably, it proceeds to ignore the half of the tenets that can be used to counterbalance the exploitable ones; we've been through that on the forums, but suffice to say that the text would have a damned difficult time arguing against not eating humans or The Veil Shall Not Be Lifted. Especially so for that last one, because it spends so much time pulling for the status quo that it wouldn't be able to exist without it.<br /> <br /> The Changing Ways sidebar is still a slap in the face. And it still makes for a less good version of Revised.<br /> <br /> We get some prominent septs that really do not make it seem like it's a reboot, as they name check some prominent ones from Caerns: Places of Power and Rage Across the Amazon, with the last example referencing the war that the Garou were waging there up until recently. There's some hand-waving about how the BSDs managed to move an entire hive.<br /> <br /> Moots are now apparently more occasional things than regular meetings to revitalize the caern. Seems unnecessary. The text hits the &quot;Garou getting together magnifies their Rage!&quot; drum pretty hard. It makes me long for the days of a certain rite from CoG Revised. This is how low W5 is, especially considering that there's no tenet against the Rite of Clouds and Rain in this edition, and it'd be easier to mechanically define it.<br /> <br /> Harano is somehow both watered down as a game concept yet also made more severe. In prior editions, just to recount things for potential readers who didn't know, it only happened under extreme circumstances and its mechanical effect, while a character was afflicted with it, was to halve every dice pool you roll unless you succeeded at a scene-by-scene Willpower roll (tn 7). There were also mechanics to recover if you did something significant. The presentation in W5 makes it a one-way slide with no chance of fighting back and also undersells what it is by not talking about how it's a product of the extremes of being Garou.<br /> <br /> Hauglosk is presented as the opposite, though it's noted that, again, in legacy, Harano can result in a sudden burst of of activity in response to what the Garou is going through. In general, those psychological states are probably a bit too cumbersome to make a regular part of the game the way Vampire deals with Humanity. Also, Hauglosk is another one of those &quot;guess what the people who made this game think of you?&quot; things, and the answer to that guessing game is... not very great, since the storytelling chapter likens it to falling down the ecofascist pipeline and together with certain comments made about various attempts to write the Get make it pretty apparent how bad it is. Again, well trod by now, but it needs to be repeated as long as the W5 crowd keeps denying that it's the case.<br /> <br /> The auspice and tribe descriptions have glyphs associated with them, but remember, Garou history is only ever transmitted orally! And it's not like oral history could, say, preserve a 100,000 year memory of where stars used to appear over the horizon!<br /> <br /> The Black Furies are now the new Get of Fenris, the Bone Gnawers' tendency to help the down and out people they live around is only communicated through their tribal patron's ban, CoGs are oriented around mystery instead of peace, the Ghost Council seems okay hanging out with BSDs for information, and not even the Silver Fangs have any sense of history to them. But at least they have The Legend of Polk High! And everyone has plenty of musicians in the Galliards!<br /> <br /> Chargen and Traits spends way too much time giving a rundown of the 1-5 dots and cracking jokes. You know, if you wanted to make your game seem modern, you might not want to copy the format that the games had in the 90s. Just... Saiyan.<br /> <br /> People will swear up and down that Appearance isn't a thing but much like CoD, it just got folded into Charisma. Also not a thing that makes you think of a modern game: Charisma including your looks!<br /> <br /> Composure 5 has a standout dated reference with 5 dots being &quot;You probably wouldn't have paid 44 billion USD for twitter&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's not an example of Composure 5, book. That's an example of Composure 2, maybe even 1.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of finger-wagging about the applicability of Specialties. While I can get where it comes from in some cases, like wanting it to not apply always, ragging on people for a fighting style that they'll probably use often seems like a very 90s thing to do.<br /> <br /> Academics jumps from talking about BS degrees straight to doctoral ones. That felt like a bit of whiplash.<br /> <br /> Backgrounds and Merits. Why Both?<br /> <br /> Loresheets only allow you to take levels of one Loresheet at chargen. That's not how Loresheets should be used as a concept. I know, because I read Weapons of the Gods ~20 years ago. The structure of the concept is meant to engage a character in various parts of the setting, and multiple avenues of that may, in fact, be necessary.<br /> <br /> Resources notes that high Resources can have your character involved with despoiling of the world and that it could be hypocritical. Oh, now you have a problem with capital, book. How convenient.<br /> <br /> Spirit Pact notes that Ghost Council and Red Talons Garou make pacts with banes. (Picks up flamethrower, ignites it) Whelp, time to burn this motherfucker down.<br /> <br /> Renown is 1-5 and purchased; the chagrin process for when you act against it reduces its effective rating until you're sufficiently more like your heroic image or what have you. Like everything else, the descriptions of Renown take the time to remind you that Garou are horrible and cannot succeed after every description.<br /> <br /> Taking a moment again, let's all give the sidebar on Wolf touchstones a hearty fuck you for not knowing very much about wolves beyond lifespan and that they operate in different ways, which the text interprets as wholly lacking volition in a number of ways.<br /> <br /> XP is based on multiples of traits to raise it. Once again, very 90s. So modern. Very updated. Also, it's the developer's interpretation of it, so instead of current rating x multiple it's new rating x multiple. Milestone improvements are a brief suggestion.<br /> <br /> Much like Weapons of the Gods, there's a suggestion to make a relationship map. I find the one that's sketched up in the book distracting but also kind of hilarious because all but one of the names are culled from Rage. Like, not just W:tA or anything, but characters that showed up in Rage, the card game. Anna Kliminiski is noted as the mentor of Zachary (Ellison), Susan (Anthony) and Syntax operated under Jonas (Albrecht) and Raina (Fader - a Corax, and the only non-Rage character), and there was also Thomas (Kachina) as a bit of the odd man out. Note that Thomas was Younger Brother in past editions but a Galestalker here; everyone else is of the same tribe.<br /> <br /> Again, not exactly selling this as a reboot. Especially since there actually are hints of past characterization there - the Shadow Lords treat everyone as objects, Thomas doesn't like Syntax (a Glass Walker), Syntax is playing a dance around the Shadow Lord, and Susan Anthony, who was a kind of a (figurative) maneater, views Thomas as an object as well. In fact, everyone seems to share this standpoint about him, which comes across as really, really unfortunate given that the character was, you know, Younger Brother (and there's no real indication that he's not of mixed Italian - Native American descent anymore, if you happen to know the name and tribe associations).<br /> <br /> But it would line up completely with, you know, everything in James Sembrano's recounting of their treatment during this project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T06:08:57-07:00","id":1544388,"title":"","content":"The Litany section is insulting. The way it is presented gives zero room for its actual use and it mostly focuses on few tenets. Philodox is yet again treated as a non-entity of an auspice.<br /> <br /> What makes me laugh, though, is that there is no mention of the Veil or cannibalism tenets being the exception to the rule. But in SN veil suddenly matters.<br /> <br /> Minor correction, though, Younger Brother is (mostly) the same as Gale Stalkers.<br /> <br /> Alongside how Thomas is being treated, I really do not like the Gale Stalker ban. If you want to distance the tribe from their old patron, maybe actually look for things North Wind WOULD favour.<br /> <br /> It also still ties the tribe heavily to Indigenous northern people just from the glyph alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T17:46:08-07:00","id":1544444,"title":"","content":"And now for the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J548XM9-jKU\" target=\"_blank\">Rules</a> chapter.<br /> <br /> The system doesn't go back to the old days of variable target numbers, but suggests that it might change from its fixed target of 6 on occasion. A light version of stunts from Exalted exists, where if you have a well-thought out response or action, you can reduce the difficulty (read: the number of successes required just for basic success on the roll) or possibly even just succeed. Health and Willpower operate as per Storytelling rather than Storyteller, so immediately, there's a great big compromise to the durability of the Garou, who could previously get mountains of soak dice. Also, it makes you roll temporary values, because apparently some lick fan wanted symmetry with all WP rolls and Dominate or something.<br /> <br /> Like the CoD, only two types of modifier to rolls typically get used, and they're dedicated to specific circumstances. Difficulty is for external circumstances, while dice pool alterations are internal, character-based ones. You can also <s>Take 10</s> Take Half on a roll to just succeed if no one wants to bother with potential swing on a roll. We're also told that W5 will let you do this in combat, something apparently frowned upon in V5 and H5, kind of like how Forsaken can just dispatch less powerful adversaries in certain forms in W:tF 2e. 10s are not doubled... unless you roll a pair of them, kind of. These are &quot;critical wins&quot; and how is it that modeling yourself after D&amp;D is more modern, exactly? I'm calling that as very old school, if not 90s.<br /> <br /> Not meeting the difficulty is introduced as winning with a cost. Well, at least one thing from no earlier than last decade got in. Willpower allows you to reroll three failed dice instead of getting a success. Is there a reason to spend it?<br /> <br /> Combat and most social interactions are modeled as &quot;conflict&quot;. This grinds my gears on turbo, because it's like Exalted 2e social combat speedrunning Willpower loss, and I also wholly reject the notion that social interaction is an exact mirror of tearing someone apart, or perhaps just beating or shooting them. Instead of having a Defense rating like in CoD, the system opted for a defense dice pool that you don't have to set aside actions to have. Getting ganged up on will eat away at said pool, but it's still reflexive. Combat, at any rate, is now a jousting contest where you want to get more successes than the opponent, like Shadowrun melee combat. Except that you still have to split your pool to attack multiple targets.<br /> <br /> Initiative isn't used, instead having an order of action that follows from which action you use. V5 also set up the mandate of not making combat last longer than three turns, so if you came here to tear apart a crowd of foes, the writers want you to know that if you had fun doing this before, it was wrong and bad, and you should feel bad.<br /> <br /> Damage has been flattened into superficial and aggravated. What, exactly, those two are depends on how tough you are; humans now take agg from almost everything that can break the skin or bones, and that matters for them, while for monsters, a lot of things that might have been lethal are now superficial. Also, Garou in other forms can make Rage checks to heal damage... any type of damage. Even aggravated. Crinos heals double time. This doesn't really have the feel of potentially dying but making a come back with a Rage roll to recover from the damage on the brink of death, though.<br /> <br /> Also, someone was apparently incensed at the existence of Master of Fire, and went out of their way to emphasize fire being Serious Bad News, even though Garou have always had Kiss of Helios in the Gift section.<br /> <br /> Feats of Strength now rely on Athletics. Yes, they kept the one dot &quot;you can crush a can!&quot; feat. Amazing use of word count and space, that.<br /> <br /> Rage is no longer related to a permanent value, and runs one to five. Technically 0 to 5, because losing the wolf can happen really often, which is dumb, because they don't let vampires eliminate that last bit of Hunger unless they kill someone to do it. Rage checks can result in a rapid loss of it, since each die has a 50% chance to do so. Also, like Nightmare from Changeling, having Rage replaces dice in actions with Rage dice, which is basically the only manifestation of botching that remains in the system, and it can get you on a 1 or a 2, two of which will auto-fail you. How I long for a wild die system instead.<br /> <br /> Since agg is the new lethal, you don't die immediately from being incapacitated with it, and can instead try to heal it, at the cost of two 50% Rage loss rolls per level. While knocked out from agg and out, you'll only die if you get hit by fire or silver. Or, like, someone uses lots of explosives.<br /> <br /> Silver is a special case on its own, because it gives you Rage for every level you suffer. This is presumably why Silver Claws burns you for a level of damage each turn, accomplishing a similar end through an annoying means. At any rate, this is probably a good time to mention that you take Willpower damage if you're at Rage 5 and you gain Rage. Combined with the &quot;Stamina does not soak, it just adds more HLs&quot; model of play, this means that you're going to run out of WP fast if someone is using silver, unless you make a bunch of Rage checks. Homid and lupus don't take damage from silver.<br /> <br /> The Five Forms are still here, but not really. As has been mentioned, no one involved in the production of the book apparently can tell the different between a wolf and German Shepherd, apparently, which harms the work via ignorance. The persistent insistence that Hispo is a dire wolf is also a bugbear that I'll refer the reader to the 1e AD&amp;D Monster Manual about to clear up that mess. Glabro gains a lot because the forms all have blanket bonuses to all physical tests; lupus loses the most, because it use to be fast. Hispo was quizzically given the role of overland movement ace, which isn't good on any level (like the Veil, for starters).<br /> <br /> Crinos. Crinos, Crinos, Crinos. The Vampire stans have had their eyes fixed on you for so long that they've lost sight of everything but stat boosts and a lame attempt to balance the game. Some even believe that limiting the time in Crinos is the key to making the game play more like a &quot;traditional&quot; werewolf, because it's the &quot;win button&quot; or something.<br /> <br /> If that's the case, why is it that no werewolf in a movie gets punted out of the form for the rest of the night that they go on their rampage? Because according to the rules, Crinos induces frenzy, frenzy burns out all of your Rage after increasing it to 5 for the duration (hardly a good thing, recall; any increase in Rage is still going to hit your temporary Willpower), and it never lasts for more than one scene. Shorter, if you run out of targets. After that, you lose the wolf. So tell me, then, if you're brave enough to get a login and reply to this post on this forum: how does this model the nightly rampage of the Wolfman and company? You know, where they're rampaging out for the entire night?<br /> <br /> And you're only worried about this because... someone might play mini golf or have tea in Crinos, and you think that looks silly? Or is it because you think the game is broken because of the stat boosts that vampires don't match? In this game, which is about something vastly different than V:tM and has never treated Crinos as the end-all, be-all, because there are a number of Gifts that alter it in some fashion.<br /> <br /> So fuck temporary Crinos. It's clear that any intention for game balance or modeling of fiction has gone far, far awry to appease some bizarre form of concern trolling about a game.<br /> <br /> Harano and Hauglosk are an annoying, double jeopardy, feel bad mechanic. You're offered some kind of risk and reward mechanic for being able to refill all your Willpower or Rage depending on which point you voluntarily take, but since you can't reduce them without a particular Loresheet at five dots, it's clearly not much of a reward. It just makes Werewolf more like Changeling, if you were in a Changeling chronicle where you were speedrunning accumulation of Banality and couldn't reduce temporary Banality with Glamour.<br /> <br /> The Delirium does have a condensed chart with only three necessary entries. Finally, something that's caught back up with 2005 in gaming. It tries to chip away at the rationalization that humans typically engage in when they see recorded media of Crinos, though, so it's clearly trying to open up the SI to act on werewolves even though they don't really have the numbers, expertise, or equipment to do this.<br /> <br /> Shit, do I hate the forms in this game. Nothing learned from Forsaken 2e beyond &quot;Crinos blenderizes low-threat targets easily&quot;, and the only concern the writing seems to have is hemming in the capabilities of every form to a very, very irritating degree. It tries to set some of them up as having a purpose, but gives little to no support for this. At least lupus, it seems, can still communicate with other Garou when they lose the wolf. Small graces, cold comforts. I'm hating something that's making me think better of CoG Revised, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T21:45:16-07:00","id":1544446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544444#post1544444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rage is no longer related to a permanent value, and runs one to five. Technically 0 to 5, because losing the wolf can happen really often, which is dumb, because they don't let vampires eliminate that last bit of Hunger unless they kill someone to do it. Rage checks can result in a rapid loss of it, since each die has a 50% chance to do so. Also, like Nightmare from Changeling, having Rage replaces dice in actions with Rage dice, which is basically the only manifestation of botching that remains in the system, and it can get you on a 1 or a 2, two of which will auto-fail you. How I long for a wild die system instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage in W5 is so baffling. I know I've ranted about it before, but the beauty of Rage in legacy was that it served as its own punishment. Too little and you risked not being able to death rage. Too much and you were a threat to everyone. It isn't even like they removed the alienating factor from Rage, because Rage dice exist and are even WORSE than the Curse. The Curse at least lets you keep your wits about you, but Rage dice mean you might randomly just break shit. And the more you have the worse it gets as you have to use ALL Rage dice at once.<br /> <br /> This means that, though the Curse doesn't exist, the garou of W5 are no better with humanity. Only that now there isn't even the reprieve of an auspice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544444#post1544444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crinos. Crinos, Crinos, Crinos. The Vampire stans have had their eyes fixed on you for so long that they've lost sight of everything but stat boosts and a lame attempt to balance the game. Some even believe that limiting the time in Crinos is the key to making the game play more like a &quot;traditional&quot; werewolf, because it's the &quot;win button&quot; or something.<br /> <br /> If that's the case, why is it that no werewolf in a movie gets punted out of the form for the rest of the night that they go on their rampage? Because according to the rules, Crinos induces frenzy, frenzy burns out all of your Rage after increasing it to 5 for the duration (hardly a good thing, recall; any increase in Rage is still going to hit your temporary Willpower), and it never lasts for more than one scene. Shorter, if you run out of targets. After that, you lose the wolf. So tell me, then, if you're brave enough to get a login and reply to this post on this forum: how does this model the nightly rampage of the Wolfman and company? You know, where they're rampaging out for the entire night?<br /> <br /> And you're only worried about this because... someone might play mini golf or have tea in Crinos, and you think that looks silly? Or is it because you think the game is broken because of the stat boosts that vampires don't match? In this game, which is about something vastly different than V:tM and has never treated Crinos as the end-all, be-all, because there are a number of Gifts that alter it in some fashion.<br /> <br /> So fuck temporary Crinos. It's clear that any intention for game balance or modeling of fiction has gone far, far awry to appease some bizarre form of concern trolling about a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck, when I talk about non-WtA werewolf fans, they don't want a short crinos. They want the man and beast to be a sort of (pop culture) Jekyll and Hyde sort of thing.<br /> <br /> I find the 'mini-golf crinos looks too silly' argument to be an excuse and the fact that crinos is so strong with full control the actual reason. Especially stronger than the vampires, even though they fight VERY different foes as you said.<br /> <br /> And, I mean, Bloodlines' werewolf scene is iconic BECAUSE the werewolf is so scary and strong. You can't wait it out, you must deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T00:28:25-07:00","id":1544447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If that's the case, why is it that no werewolf in a movie gets punted out of the form for the rest of the night that they go on their rampage? Because according to the rules, Crinos induces frenzy, frenzy burns out all of your Rage after increasing it to 5 for the duration (hardly a good thing, recall; any increase in Rage is still going to hit your temporary Willpower) </div> </div> </div>You can't really gain Rage during combat. It says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Provocation, Harm, or Humiliation: If the Garou suffers harm, pain, or other emotional or physical agitation, they gain a point of Rage, maximum one per<br /> turn. <b>Note that once combat begins, most damage and injury don\u2019t yield additional Rage</b>; low-level provocation, such as insults and trash talk, don\u2019t provoke further Rage, either. </div> </div> </div>And I think you have to run this game that way. You can't get Rage during combat and combat has to be &quot;three turns and you're done&quot;.<br /> <br /> First, why no Rage-gain during combat...? It's all about the Crinos-Form and Frenzy. Say you enter the Crinos Form in combat willingly. Then you have to pay 1 WP per turn or enter Frenzy. The first hurdle here is that if you were to get into a situation where you can't pay 1 WP and enter Frenzy... you're fucked. But if you include the idea of gaining Rage during combat, that would mean that once you enter Frenzy, you're in Crinos and gain Rage 5. But during Frenzy you can't use Gifts and you're stuck in Crinos. So no Rage-checks from Gifts or shifting. Aside from Regeneration you're stuck with Rage 5, so any Rage-gain would immediately turn into WP-damage. And then both in the former scenario of entering Frenzy because you can't pay the WP-cost or in the latter scenario where Rage-gain while having Rage 5 creates WP-damage, you run into the same issue: After you've killed the source of the Frenzy you have to do a WP-test whether you're about to try to kill everything in sight. But with the WP-damage involved in this process, you can't give Rage during combat because then you would almost guarantee that the Frenzy will go out of control.<br /> <br /> Second, why the three turns and you're done...? Since gaining Rage during combat could lead to problems, you gain little to no Rage during combat. Of course, the first obvious issue is that narratively it's a bit lackluster (like a player asking &quot;What do you mean I don't get Rage when I get attacked in combat...?&quot;). But the other is that with that in mind between shifting, regenerating and using Gifts, even going into combat with Rage 5 might get used up pretty quickly... unless you stick to &quot;three turns and you're done&quot;. That's why I was so baffled by the Isle of Splintered Dreams suggestion of setting up a combat-scene that mandated 8 turns or more.<br /> <br /> And finally, the biggest irony of all is that W5 has created a solution that is anything but. Even if the complaint is that you don't like the idea of Garou being in Crinos for lengthy periods of time, the system of W5 is pushing for the opposite extreme. And we know that this came up during playtesting. Outstar talked about how in one of her playtesting-sessions nobody shifted into Crinos. And if you're dealing with particularly risk-averse players, it's obvious why they would never shift into Crinos. Especially if you're stingy with giving out Rage, you might refrain from shifting, using Gifts and regenerating because you don't want to be caught with your pants down due to losing your wolf.<br /> <br /> Of course, even these risk-averse players might get further confirmation that they should avoid Crinos because of Frenzy. Because &quot;severe provocations&quot; can trigger Frenzy-checks. What are &quot;severe provocations&quot;, you might wonder...? Who knows. It's all up to the ST to decide that.<br /> <br /> The only concrete example of Frenzy-checks is the harming of Touchstones. And so hurting Touchstones is a double-whammy because the PC has to do a Frenzy-check <i>and </i>a Harano-check. And it's quite the thing what W5 supplements suggest you do with that. In both Scent of Decay and Red Tundra it's suggested that when you're dealing with a Pentex-front, you should take players' Touchstones and make them employees of the Pentex-front the PCs are about to attack. Like when it says in Scent of Decay:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Side Hustle<br /> Storytellers looking to add some personal stakes to the story should consider an unexpected encounter with a pack member\u2019s Touchstone or another Relationship Map connection. The fulfillment center is always hiring, and bumping into the character will complicate this scene no matter the approach the pack takes. The Touchstone took the job because they need more money, either to supplement their regular income, or because they lost their job and didn\u2019t tell the pack member yet.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Of course, neither Scent of Decay (like in this excerpt) nor Red Tundra end up addressing the full mechanical consequences of putting a Touchstone into harm's way like that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T05:42:46-07:00","id":1544455,"title":"","content":"I'd say it needed more playtesting, but if you have problems at the top, no amount of playtesting would be enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T06:39:12-07:00","id":1544461,"title":"","content":"Alone the way they went about deemphasizing the Umbra in W5...<br /> <br /> If it wasn't already clear enough by removing it as a natural ability for Garou and making it a Rite. Let's remember that when you lose the wolf, you can't use Gifts or Rites. So, imagine if the PCs have one guy who can do the Rite of the Shadow Passage, they go into the Umbra, fight some Spirits and the guy who knows the Rite loses the wolf. In the real world, that would already be disruptive enough because you have to wait till this PC can howl at the moon. But they're not in the real world, they're in the Umbra. And according to W5, in every scene after the first the PCs have to spend a point of WP or suffer aggravated damage. In other words, in the scenario mentioned before the PCs are simply dead. All because the one PC who knows the Rite of Shadow Passage lost the wolf. Doesn't that sound like fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T06:40:25-07:00","id":1544462,"title":"","content":"Every single time I consider WEREWOLF 5th edition (and these days that isn\u2019t very often) it keeps striking me as a case of somehow embodying the very worst of all possible worlds - as a sequel, as a reboot, as a remake.<br /> <br /> It would be quite impressive, if only it weren\u2019t such a tragic case of mistreatment and misunderstanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T13:22:38-07:00","id":1544491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544461#post1544461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alone the way they went about deemphasizing the Umbra in W5...<br /> <br /> If it wasn't already clear enough by removing it as a natural ability for Garou and making it a Rite. Let's remember that when you lose the wolf, you can't use Gifts or Rites. So, imagine if the PCs have one guy who can do the Rite of the Shadow Passage, they go into the Umbra, fight some Spirits and the guy who knows the Rite loses the wolf. In the real world, that would already be disruptive enough because you have to wait till this PC can howl at the moon. But they're not in the real world, they're in the Umbra. And according to W5, in every scene after the first the PCs have to spend a point of WP or suffer aggravated damage. In other words, in the scenario mentioned before the PCs are simply dead. All because the one PC who knows the Rite of Shadow Passage lost the wolf. Doesn't that sound like fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ...?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the point. Between the ST section comparing hauglosk to ecofascism and just fascism in general and the rants about attempts to make the Get of Fenris work in earlier iterations of W5, I can only assume that the editor believes that we're all garbage people who deserve to be shunned for liking a game he didn't like and saw as utterly evil. The alternative - that he thinks the Get of Fenris existed without being written in a certain way and that fictional characters should be punished for the way they were written - would probably be even more uncharitable, as it would assume that he doesn't know the difference between reality and pretend, and would also probably only have targeted the Get. Instead, the choice we get is Harano or Hauglosk - stop playing the game, or accept that you're the worst.<br /> <br /> (Meanwhile, don't ask what your sire was up to in the 30s and 40s... or the 1860s... or the late 15th century to the mid 16th century...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T20:02:27-07:00","id":1544529,"title":"","content":"Umbra? Not yet. Storytelling!<br /> <br /> The book gives assurances that the ST isn't a dictator. That seems like a very 90s assurance.<br /> <br /> We're introduced to Chronicle Tenets! They get more consideration than Litany Tenets! And depending on which ones your ST chooses, you may be facing more or fewer incidences of Hauglosk, because going against those tenets will cause the accumulation of the Feel Bad Trackers. That seems like it's trying to to seem more open with play options than the book actually sets down.<br /> <br /> Themes come next. A lot of them are hitting some of the points that have already been driven into the ground, and some of which don't even feel like they fit because a lot of them don't apply in a setting where Garou can just bone among their own and not have to deal with the dance around the former first tenet of the litany. While a lot of the world might be against them, it is, in fact, possible to have a birth family among pack members. Much of the tension there just deflated from where it was down to normal levels. This kind of derails the emphasis on the pack that the other themes try to bang into the ground.<br /> <br /> Then there's the section entitled &quot;The Real Problem With the Garou&quot;. As noted, I can't help but think that at least some of this is spillover targeted at legacy players. It really bangs on the &quot;Garou are really good at violence!&quot; drum, presenting them as ineffectual by other means. Well, I suppose if you cut many of those out, they don't quite do as well, but even then, there are a vast number of Garou that have access to Animal Magnetism to boost general social rolls (not just because it's in a number of common splats, but also because there aren't really many Gifts to get). The spirit world is also treated as a weight around their neck rather than a vital piece of their existence and potential place to find allies and means to deal with problems.<br /> <br /> Some basic story structuring and game advice, like session 0 and goals, follows. There's a note that the game can get gory, but with this iteration, I'm not completely seeing it, since it's waiting with a watch to take away Crinos... and all of your shapeshifting and other powers, most likely. Much is made about various sources of conflict, which the game notes as having the potential to cause strain with the players if it goes on for too long, but it gives no advice about how to deal with that if you trip over it.<br /> <br /> Then it comes to the Umbra. The most significant portion of this chapter is the sidebar that notes that animism is a real world belief system, which is broadly true (it tends to be an anthropological waste basket of classification, if I'm not mistaken, where anyone considered to be &quot;pre-modern&quot; gets described as &quot;animistic&quot;). Critically, it doesn't let W:tA lay down its vision of animism as true for the game setting. That's the beginning of the problems, where any proximity to the Umbra that the Garou had was basically scrubbed away for this edition; they're not considered to be natives of it, and the game takes the time to kick you again by having spirits blaming the Garou for everything instead of being ready to help them do something.<br /> <br /> In &quot;Appeal to the Senses&quot;, we get one of the few times that the book tries to get into the heads of beings with wolf senses. Not the wolf-born, though; if that were the case, it would note something important in addition to the phrase &quot;the Garou are no longer *just* human...&quot;. There's a slight bit more attention given to spirits, and how their state and activity level should indicate something about the Umbra. I guess if you can't just go check for yourself, that would be more important.<br /> <br /> There's some call for letting consequences be the concern for actions. That tracks with old stuff regarding bad decisions made by Garou, but it lacks the larger scale that those things can happen on. Antagonists are given an &quot;alignment&quot; of sorts, with the axes of Individual to Systemic and Active to Passive; I probably would have changed the latter with Enemy to Rival, personally, denoting whether something is part of your society and a nominal ally that just doesn't like you or, well, BSDs (don't believe their lies!).<br /> <br /> The game kind of goes into its own ass about Three Act Structure. As a counterpoint, I'll just post <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_story_structures\" target=\"_blank\">this link</a>. And also <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kish%C5%8Dtenketsu\" target=\"_blank\">this one</a>.<br /> <br /> XP and rewards, straight out of the 90s!<br /> <br /> Problems Werewolves Face - if you thought that the book was done kicking you for maybe liking the game or the characters, buckle up. It's going to get bumpy, here.<br /> <br /> The first point, that Garou are imperfect guardians with an ancient purpose to defend the realm of Gaia, seems innocent enough. That Garou are a bit isolated could be, too, though the descriptions used prompt one to also think of the X-Men - guardians of a world that hates and fears you!<br /> <br /> Then we hit &quot;The Wyrm is winning because it has adapted&quot;, and a lot of things go sideways. It's knocking Garou back to where they were even before the first edition core. Forget W5 being a less good version of Revised, it's also a terrible version of 1e and 2e. Also, I'd like to point out that per the old lore, the Wyrm didn't adapt; it can just easily corrupt and suborn the structures that the Weaver produces. But who knows if we'll ever get lengthy discussion of Triatic Wyrms and the psychological break of a cosmic entity. As usual, I suspect not; I'd say not anytime soon, but Shattered Nation previews don't leave me very hopeful.<br /> <br /> We get that they're creatures of Rage and spirit, wolf and human, and could have fucking fooled me, book. You talk like them as if they're not part spirit with that whole &quot;foreign to the Umbra, hated by the spirits&quot; crap.<br /> <br /> There's a somewhat confused and garbled paragraph on the importance of Renown among the &quot;fractured, isolated&quot; Garou and their broken society. Setting aside that Renown is only really possible in a more cohesive setup, it's trying to pump something back up (tale-telling and deeds) after it's been trashing it the whole book.<br /> <br /> Werewolf society walks a perilous line? Well, yes, I suppose if you delete or ignore the half of the Litany that stabilizes it, it would. This deserves a <a href=\"https://youtu.be/2YzHTt2Pns4?t=262\" target=\"_blank\">wanking gesture</a>. (Don't worry, it's just a Berserk '97 outtake.)<br /> <br /> The Werewolf instinct is to Rage and destroy - yet another point trying to hammer you down about Garou frequently harming those around them when they try to do something, and a cry to not do anything, because doing something would be bad. You monster. I think this book needs to take some advice from the X-Men '97 cartoon (or real life) about the continual and constant effects of outrage and callouts. Also, apparently the Glory and Honor tribes kick sand in the face of the Wisdom tribes, that bunch of spirit-nerds.<br /> <br /> Umbra, next time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T00:12:59-07:00","id":1544536,"title":"","content":"Sooo, does the ST section give ANY reason one might actually WANT to play a garou? XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T00:53:04-07:00","id":1544538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544536#post1544536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooo, does the ST section give ANY reason one might actually WANT to play a garou? XD</div> </div> </div> </div>It's teetering on the edge of a Lunars 1e situation, I think.<br /> <br /> &quot;Don't assume that the characters will be idiots!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...My, what a strange way to try and give advice.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's like that, but instead of idiots as such, it's about not being glory-hungry murder machines. Which... I don't know if the books realize this, but that's what the first edition was about. And the second. And the third. And the 20th anniversary books with the Eighth Sign of the Phoenix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T02:53:28-07:00","id":1544539,"title":"","content":"When it comes to ST-advice, we gotta bring up this bit from the Frenzy-section:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The werewolf cannot themselves use Gifts, however, and must keep acting out frenzy, or the player must yield control of the character to the Storyteller. </div> </div> </div>I couldn't believe my eyes the first time I saw that during the previews. GMs who do this kind of thing are material for rpg-horror-stories-threads. In this day and age where a more collaborative process is favored, it's insane to put something like this in your corebook.<br /> <br /> And of course, a player could potentially become frustrated with Frenzy in this game. If your PC has entered Frenzy and then after killing the cause for the Frenzy fails the WP-test, Frenzy can turn into this lengthy scene where you have to play out how this PC is gonna try killing everything in sight.<br /> <br /> As for the actual Storytelling-chapter... It's no wonder that once you get past all the complaints about how bad Garou are, what is actually left? Playing traditionalist Garou. Caring abour Renown, fighting the Wyrm, protecting caerns... And that's why it doesn't work: All these complaints are <i>about </i>WtA but not addressed <i>within </i>W5. The only thing W5 has going for it as a big change to how it plays is this giant heap of punitive mechanics. Being a Garou is less fun than in previous editions. Alone the fact that W5 is a game with a doom-spiral in the form of Harano/Hauglosk, an inescapable downward spiral that will render your character &quot;unplayable&quot; according to the game. I think this is the only WOD-game that is this extreme. You can't lose dots in Harano/Hauglosk, you can only ever accrue more of them as your character gets closer and closer to &quot;death&quot;. But then at the same time, as I mentioned at the start here: You're still just doing the same shit. The only way I can make sense of this is that this edition was written with the idea of &quot;Garou suck and we're gonna make sure you get the message.&quot;.<br /> <br /> One particular mechanic in how it's presented also doesn't work: Chronicle Tenets. I don't think there's enough emphasis in the description that Chronicle Tenets are linked to Hauglosk. Chronicle Tenets aren't just this general &quot;preference for genre emulation or dramatic irony, elevate a moral direction, or plant a flag for personal taste or real-life player concerns&quot; as the book puts it.<br /> <br /> Take Apocalypse Radicals:<ul><li>Do not cling to the old ways</li> <li>Never kill an outsider</li> <li>Vengeance must be served\u200b</li> </ul>If you were to take these Tenets, the game would be saying that the moment these PCs do something that would be considered more traditional, they would be going down the path of Hauglosk. How does that make sense in the way Hauglosk is described? The other problem is when you have these Tenets that overlap. &quot;Never kill and outsider&quot; and &quot;Vengeance must be served&quot; might well apply to a scenario at the same time. And what do you do then? The mechanic is &quot;Here's a line in the sand and if you cross it, do a Hauglosk-check.&quot;. Narratively you can play a lot with conflicting PC values and principles within a lot of games, of course, but this particular system becomes muddled and unworkable when you do that here. And an even worse example of exactly that is the suggested example in the written out description:<br /> <br /> Rural Gothic:<ul><li>Punish the guilty\u200b</li> <li>Everyone deserves a second chance</li> <li>Never harm the innocent</li> </ul>When things get muddled like this, it all comes back once again to ST fiat. And that's another thing that comes up time and time again in the W5 corebook: This blind trust that the ST will simply work it all out in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T10:27:19-07:00","id":1544573,"title":"","content":"There was so much to deal with that I did forget to note that the &quot;act out the frenzy or else&quot; is very 90s. Writers should have checked up on Limit and Limit Break, at the very least; that'd get them past the 90s, maybe even to something vaguely modern for this &quot;modernization&quot; of the game mechanics. Which mostly just seem to involve more dice rolls for healing than anyone ever rolled for soak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T17:03:36-07:00","id":1544607,"title":"","content":"Now, for the sum of all fears, the Umbra and Spirits chapter.<br /> <br /> Right from the start, it keeps calling it the Spirit Wilds and mentions that it's the lens that they see it as. So, some fool has attempted to make this game work like Mage, complete with the vidare concept. Thanks, I hate it!<br /> <br /> Much like Mage, this section is agonizingly non-committal about what it's talking about. The Umbra could be this, or it could be that; Gaia could be the spirit of the Earth, or could be larger than that; the Triat could be a metaphysical trinity, or it could be the Triat that we're more familiar with. From listening to Mage the Podcast, I've learned that this is something that's all over Mage books about cosmology; the hosts even noted that Werewolf books were refreshingly direct about their details. So, we're falling and falling further from what makes Werewolf Werewolf, here.<br /> <br /> Treating Garou as more like Mage also extends to the forced introduction of its attempts to expel or kill them, and this is also noted as a thing about the supposed era of the Apocalypse. How it's framed, however, also makes it sound like it was meant to be a change in a continuation rather than from a reboot. It exists right down to the claim of there being no universal truths. Great. Now we have to play in the Mage Umbra.<br /> <br /> This is so up in the air that I'm not even sure that reading these pages is productive in any sense of the word. Whatever you find is now up to heavy interpretation, which I don't really feel makes it matter at all. There's also this tidbit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Umbra cannot be mapped... </div> </div> </div>(Looks over to the Corax book and its &quot;Umbral Maps&quot; Background)<br /> <br /> Sure, Jan.<br /> <br /> This &quot;it depends...&quot; attitude gets repetitive in a hurry, and ends everything with a ritual statement of non-commitment like it's MatPat talking about FNAF. Some details that were present in prior editions exist in the margins of its wild flailing to avoid seeming biased to anything at all. There's a contrasting comparison of how a building might appear in the Umbra (or not) that could fit in fairly well with said older material.<br /> <br /> Getting into the Umbra is still called Stepping Sideways. How this happens is also made to be up to interpretation, with a very Mage-like explanation of one possible reason why going in as a pack is easier being &quot;more will causes reality to yield!&quot; The rules for what happens inside are described by a text box as &quot;impressionistic&quot;, which seems like they're just trying to cover up for how much material this book doesn't have in it and how they want to not answer any questions like in a Mage book. Also, instead of having spiritual energies within, the text describes surviving in the Umbra as a matter of being sustained by will. Thought and emotion casting a metaphysical shadow that is the Umbra are an assumption that is mostly default; forget about this being the soul of the world that exists beyond you but containing you, it's all about the impressions of living beings.<br /> <br /> The Hierarchy of Spirits is about the same... except that spirits might apparently understand it differently, somehow. Again, hilariously noncommittal. Gaia is named primarily as a Celestine, so the game is probably just copying a lot of 1e with way too much Mage 1e thrown in. Some spirits are noted as communicating in weird ways, and the game is determined not to let Theurges know how, because it took out Spirit Speech.<br /> <br /> And that's the end. No discussion of Near Realms, the Deep Umbra, or Zones, or hint that they'll be a Thing. Simply put, this half-complete chapter doesn't belong in a Werewolf book, and insisting that this is the way that spirit matters now work means that they're probably going to give that part of the game over to Mage above everyone else. Assuming that ever gets released, anyway. I could kind of see this coming ten years ago with the &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; BS that got played down until it became the overriding mandate, but didn't quite factor in how much the group that PDX gave the WoD was going to single out W:tA as what it was going to cut out to make everything work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T18:48:42-07:00","id":1544618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544491#post1544491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's the point. Between the ST section comparing hauglosk to ecofascism</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually I'm pretty sure that hauglosk was intended to be fanatic obsession to a cause that's that's strictly speaking dosen't have to ecofascism despite the core book's instance. Like you could arage that Don Quxoite is a example of non ecofash instance of hauglosk. Like he's a kind man who's welling to fight for good cause and inspire others to follow his example.<br /> <br /> It's just that all his actions are informed by his total obsession with chivalric novels. So strong is his obsession that it actively warps his perception of reality to the piont where he sees oreges and beast where there is none, proclaim a random shaving bowl as legendary helm, pledge his undying loyalty to a random farm girl he haven't really met much less talk to and of course charging directly towards a windmill because he thought it was a giant.<br /> <br /> Like imaging the above but with a garou...<br /> <br /> Of course you just go with the purgatory answer and say that it's actually a spectral imbalance caused by the wolf totem spirit splitting into two aspects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T20:19:31-07:00","id":1544620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/ma