<div class=\"message\">Now, for the sum of all fears, the Umbra and Spirits chapter.<br /> <br /> Right from the start, it keeps calling it the Spirit Wilds and mentions that it's the lens that they see it as. So, some fool has attempted to make this game work like Mage, complete with the vidare concept. Thanks, I hate it!<br /> <br /> Much like Mage, this section is agonizingly non-committal about what it's talking about. The Umbra could be this, or it could be that; Gaia could be the spirit of the Earth, or could be larger than that; the Triat could be a metaphysical trinity, or it could be the Triat that we're more familiar with. From listening to Mage the Podcast, I've learned that this is something that's all over Mage books about cosmology; the hosts even noted that Werewolf books were refreshingly direct about their details. So, we're falling and falling further from what makes Werewolf Werewolf, here.<br /> <br /> Treating Garou as more like Mage also extends to the forced introduction of its attempts to expel or kill them, and this is also noted as a thing about the supposed era of the Apocalypse. How it's framed, however, also makes it sound like it was meant to be a change in a continuation rather than from a reboot. It exists right down to the claim of there being no universal truths. Great. Now we have to play in the Mage Umbra.<br /> <br /> This is so up in the air that I'm not even sure that reading these pages is productive in any sense of the word. Whatever you find is now up to heavy interpretation, which I don't really feel makes it matter at all. There's also this tidbit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (Looks over to the Corax book and its &quot;Umbral Maps&quot; Background)<br /> <br /> Sure, Jan.<br /> <br /> This &quot;it depends...&quot; attitude gets repetitive in a hurry, and ends everything with a ritual statement of non-commitment like it's MatPat talking about FNAF. Some details that were present in prior editions exist in the margins of its wild flailing to avoid seeming biased to anything at all. There's a contrasting comparison of how a building might appear in the Umbra (or not) that could fit in fairly well with said older material.<br /> <br /> Getting into the Umbra is still called Stepping Sideways. How this happens is also made to be up to interpretation, with a very Mage-like explanation of one possible reason why going in as a pack is easier being &quot;more will causes reality to yield!&quot; The rules for what happens inside are described by a text box as &quot;impressionistic&quot;, which seems like they're just trying to cover up for how much material this book doesn't have in it and how they want to not answer any questions like in a Mage book. Also, instead of having spiritual energies within, the text describes surviving in the Umbra as a matter of being sustained by will. Thought and emotion casting a metaphysical shadow that is the Umbra are an assumption that is mostly default; forget about this being the soul of the world that exists beyond you but containing you, it's all about the impressions of living beings.<br /> <br /> The Hierarchy of Spirits is about the same... except that spirits might apparently understand it differently, somehow. Again, hilariously noncommittal. Gaia is named primarily as a Celestine, so the game is probably just copying a lot of 1e with way too much Mage 1e thrown in. Some spirits are noted as communicating in weird ways, and the game is determined not to let Theurges know how, because it took out Spirit Speech.<br /> <br /> And that's the end. No discussion of Near Realms, the Deep Umbra, or Zones, or hint that they'll be a Thing. Simply put, this half-complete chapter doesn't belong in a Werewolf book, and insisting that this is the way that spirit matters now work means that they're probably going to give that part of the game over to Mage above everyone else. Assuming that ever gets released, anyway. I could kind of see this coming ten years ago with the &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; BS that got played down until it became the overriding mandate, but didn't quite factor in how much the group that PDX gave the WoD was going to single out W:tA as what it was going to cut out to make everything work.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least in Mage there are common landmarks, things to see and explore and expand upon.<br /> <br /> Arena of Immortals, The Well of Souls, Shard Realms, Elemental Courts. <br /> We know the rough outline of Umbral dimensions and what to expect, be it in Dark (Low) Umbra, Middle Umbra or Astral (High) Umbra.<br /> <br /> W5 Umbra might as well be nothing burger for ST to fix.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T02:01:14-07:00","id":1544634,"title":"","content":"Just like with the descriptions of Garou-history, the Umbra-descriptions are way too vague. Like what are you even supposed to get from a paragraph like this one:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In considering the animistic role of the Umbra, it may help to use a metaphor. If the physical world is an object, and the Umbra is its shadow, what\u2019s causing the illumination that results in the shadow? The truth is that no one knows. </div> </div> </div>&quot;To better understand this thing, let me offer you a metaphor. * presents metaphor * Is this thing like this metaphor? The truth is that no one knows.&quot; What the hell! Then why did you present the metaphor in the first place?!<br /> <br /> Also, on the count of &quot;animism&quot; in W5, I forgot about the sidebar in the Storytelling-chapter which... lacks a bit of self-awareness. Here's what it says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Context Matters<br /> <br /> Remember that animism is a real-world belief system practiced by millions of people in one form or another both throughout history and today. Be appropriately respectful at your table.<br /> <br /> Werewolf does not suppose the Garou\u2019s specific animistic lens is the \u201ctruth\u201d of how animism works in the game world \u2014 people\u2019s faiths and perspectives are not to be reduced to game mechanics. The relationship between the Garou and the Umbra is but a single, fictional expression of animism.\u200b </div> </div> </div>So, &quot;be appropriately respectful towards this real-world belief system - that we've determined should be constantly questioned and doubted in our game-setting&quot;. Oh, yeah, that's how you pay respect to a real-world belief...<br /> <br /> Another thing is that W5 keeps talking a big game about all this regional variety that supposedly exists in the setting. On pg 225: &quot;Differences that arise help paint a World of Darkness in which the Garou aren\u2019t a monoculture, and in which the greatest mysteries of the universe cannot be untangled, despite all of the fury and insight werewolves bring to bear.\u200b&quot; or in the Spirit Veracity sidebar on pg. 232 &quot;So, for example, a Ghost Council Garou with a Native American background may well perceive Horned Serpent in a different way than fellow Ghost Council Garou living amid Scandinavian, Iranian, or North African human cultures.\u200b&quot; or in the recent Shattered Nation supplement on pg. 7 &quot;Modern communications technology means that Garou can talk to each other easier than ever before, and so have realized that their immutable traditions and culture are often actually entirely local. Other Garou in other places do things differently.\u200b&quot; W5 keeps going on and on about all these differences and never gives any examples for this. You just get &quot;And of course, the Glass Walker in Norway has different traditions and views than the Glass Walker in Iran.&quot; But that's all you ever get! W5 in all the writing that has been presented thus far never actually has supported that idea once with any concrete examples.<br /> <br /> Of course, it doesn't help as well that all the locations for the adventures are exclusively located in North America and Europe...<br /> <br /> But the cherry on top for the Umbra chapter is &quot;Gaia's Howl&quot;. This is that central event in the setting which explains why the Umbra is in so much chaos, how there's such a high awareness of it being the Age of Apocalypse and this is why Spirits don't like Garou. So you get this section in this chapter:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whether experienced as a literal howl, a painful frisson physically felt while traversing the Gauntlet, intruding visions of Gaia in pain, or an alarming burst of taste or smell, Gaia lets her champions know that they have little time left. (See p. 224 for more information on Gaia\u2019s Howl.)\u200b </div> </div> </div>But here's the thing: This section is on pg. 224. And this section is the only time Gaia's Howl gets mentioned on that page. And the Index also tells you to go to pg 224 for the section on Gaia's Howl. In fact, there's <i>no section</i> to be found about Gaia's Howl in the Umbra chapter. It's simply missing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T07:16:06-07:00","id":1544647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544634#post1544634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, &quot;be appropriately respectful towards this real-world belief system - that we've determined should be constantly questioned and doubted in our game-setting&quot;. Oh, yeah, that's how you pay respect to a real-world belief...<br /> <br /> Another thing is that W5 keeps talking a big game about all this regional variety that supposedly exists in the setting. On pg 225: &quot;Differences that arise help paint a World of Darkness in which the Garou aren\u2019t a monoculture, and in which the greatest mysteries of the universe cannot be untangled, despite all of the fury and insight werewolves bring to bear.&quot; or in the Spirit Veracity sidebar on pg. 232 &quot;So, for example, a Ghost Council Garou with a Native American background may well perceive Horned Serpent in a different way than fellow Ghost Council Garou living amid Scandinavian, Iranian, or North African human cultures.\u200b&quot; or in the recent Shattered Nation supplement on pg. 7 &quot;Modern communications technology means that Garou can talk to each other easier than ever before, and so have realized that their immutable traditions and culture are often actually entirely local. Other Garou in other places do things differently.\u200b&quot; W5 keeps going on and on about all these differences and never gives any examples for this. You just get &quot;And of course, the Glass Walker in Norway has different traditions and views than the Glass Walker in Iran.&quot; But that's all you ever get! W5 in all the writing that has been presented thus far never actually has supported that idea once with any concrete examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>This legit reminds me of the &quot;It is pride month, you know what that means&quot;-meme. Brings something up but then refuses to elaborate on it.<br /> <br /> It isn't like it is hard to give examples for different takes. For example, European GWs might see Spider as a great mechanic spider that resembles a loom, Japanese might see a Jorogumo with needle legs and silk body and Afrucan might see Ananansi (the god) wearing a western suit.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T10:18:48-07:00","id":1544659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least in Mage there are common landmarks, things to see and explore and expand upon.<br /> <br /> Arena of Immortals, The Well of Souls, Shard Realms, Elemental Courts.<br /> We know the rough outline of Umbral dimensions and what to expect, be it in Dark (Low) Umbra, Middle Umbra or Astral (High) Umbra.<br /> <br /> W5 Umbra might as well be nothing burger for ST to fix.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, one fears what might be, or rather, not be, for M5...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544634#post1544634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just like with the descriptions of Garou-history, the Umbra-descriptions are way too vague. Like what are you even supposed to get from a paragraph like this one:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;To better understand this thing, let me offer you a metaphor. * presents metaphor * Is this thing like this metaphor? The truth is that no one knows.&quot; What the hell! Then why did you present the metaphor in the first place?!</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an urge to quote some portion of an Abridged Series where they go full Metaphorgotten, but I can't decide on which one...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, on the count of &quot;animism&quot; in W5, I forgot about the sidebar in the Storytelling-chapter which... lacks a bit of self-awareness. Here's what it says:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, &quot;be appropriately respectful towards this real-world belief system - that we've determined should be constantly questioned and doubted in our game-setting&quot;. Oh, yeah, that's how you pay respect to a real-world belief... </div> </div> </div>It also kicks the Garou about having any idea about or being correct about their own view of how spirits work. I haven't mentioned the rear-rage of bitter vampire fans for a while, but I think it may be at root here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another thing is that W5 keeps talking a big game about all this regional variety that supposedly exists in the setting. On pg 225: &quot;Differences that arise help paint a World of Darkness in which the Garou aren\u2019t a monoculture, and in which the greatest mysteries of the universe cannot be untangled, despite all of the fury and insight werewolves bring to bear.\u200b&quot; or in the Spirit Veracity sidebar on pg. 232 &quot;So, for example, a Ghost Council Garou with a Native American background may well perceive Horned Serpent in a different way than fellow Ghost Council Garou living amid Scandinavian, Iranian, or North African human cultures.\u200b&quot; or in the recent Shattered Nation supplement on pg. 7 &quot;Modern communications technology means that Garou can talk to each other easier than ever before, and so have realized that their immutable traditions and culture are often actually entirely local. Other Garou in other places do things differently.\u200b&quot; W5 keeps going on and on about all these differences and never gives any examples for this. You just get &quot;And of course, the Glass Walker in Norway has different traditions and views than the Glass Walker in Iran.&quot; But that's all you ever get! W5 in all the writing that has been presented thus far never actually has supported that idea once with any concrete examples. </div> </div> </div>I think that James Sembrano forewarned the internet of this. If it takes effort, sensitivity readers, and cultural knowledge, it probably won't be showing up, because someone at the top doesn't want to dedicate the time, effort, or money to follow through. Ahem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, it doesn't help as well that all the locations for the adventures are exclusively located in North America and Europe... </div> </div> </div>Europeans complain about WoD centering too much on the US, center it too hard on Europe!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the cherry on top for the Umbra chapter is &quot;Gaia's Howl&quot;. This is that central event in the setting which explains why the Umbra is in so much chaos, how there's such a high awareness of it being the Age of Apocalypse and this is why Spirits don't like Garou. So you get this section in this chapter:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But here's the thing: This section is on pg. 224. And this section is the only time Gaia's Howl gets mentioned on that page. And the Index also tells you to go to pg 224 for the section on Gaia's Howl. In fact, there's <i>no section</i> to be found about Gaia's Howl in the Umbra chapter. It's simply missing! </div> </div> </div>Here be Dolphin Wizards and MoEP: Lunars index pants jokes (not to be confused with Nuwisha replacing Auspice on the character sheet with &quot;Pants?&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T11:50:40-07:00","id":1544664,"title":"","content":"my idea for 5th is that the tables were turned and this generation were the ones who do go out and engage in pro active eco terrorism and that the previous generations are the Harano ridden losers who sit around guarding their caern because &quot;like, violence isnt the way.&quot;. This a reboot, do something new and be topical. A little more &quot;how to blow up a pipeline&quot; by andreas marm a lot less pacifism by inaction, feelgood nothing burgers and climate fatalism. This would solve a lot of issues with how the edition is rather aimless while also making a clean break from Revised which deconstructs the violence approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T00:28:27-07:00","id":1544710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544629#post1544629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not Don Quixote, the hypothetical Garou. Apologies for the mixup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Accepted and well as I said if you take Harono as fanatical obsession then being a over idealistic fool is equally viable result of the condition as a angry ecofash.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544664#post1544664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my idea for 5th is that the tables were turned and this generation were the ones who do go out and engage in pro active eco terrorism and that the previous generations are the Harano ridden losers who sit around guarding their caern because &quot;like, violence isnt the way.&quot;. This a reboot, do something new and be topical. A little more &quot;how to blow up a pipeline&quot; by andreas marm a lot less pacifism by inaction, feelgood nothing burgers and climate fatalism. This would solve a lot of issues with how the edition is rather aimless while also making a clean break from Revised which deconstructs the violence approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnly enough the upcoming WtE is looking to take a similar route to you're proposal although it phrased more as &quot;the new generation must act now to ensure there's a better future for both the nation and gaia&quot; than &quot;Let's blow up more pipelines and kill as many CEOs we can get our paws on&quot;.<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/dXGG39V.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/dXGG39V.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/dXGG39V.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T14:07:01-07:00","id":1544750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544634#post1544634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just like with the descriptions of Garou-history, the Umbra-descriptions are way too vague. Like what are you even supposed to get from a paragraph like this one:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;To better understand this thing, let me offer you a metaphor. * presents metaphor * Is this thing like this metaphor? The truth is that no one knows.&quot; What the hell! Then why did you present the metaphor in the first place?!<br /> <br /> !</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's worse than that. It's not even a metaphor, nor does it address the point. <br /> <br /> It starts with&quot; in considering the animistic role of the umbra&quot;, but nothing about the umbra being the shadow of the earth or what illuminates it explain anything in the role of the umbra in an animist cosmos. <br /> <br /> In fact, the attempt at making a metaphor fails.<br /> Let's say, as the overpaid writer made it, that the relationship of the umbra toward the material world is equivalent to that of a shadow of an object. <br /> <br /> That makes the umbra unimportant. A shadow is nothing to the object. By that metaphor, the umbra is merely the byproduct of the material. If we follow it, the umbra as no more impact on the material as a shadow has on the object that cast it. <br /> <br /> And for whatever illuminate it, it has even less importance toward the animist role of the umbra. <br /> <br /> The more I read such snippets of the book, the more I believe we'll end up with every author of that thing on some sort of shame list in the ttrpg industry","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T14:08:22-07:00","id":1544751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544710#post1544710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Accepted and well as I said if you take Harono as fanatical obsession then being a over idealistic fool is equally viable result of the condition as a angry ecofash.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Funnly enough the upcoming WtE is looking to take a similar route to you're proposal although it phrased more as &quot;the new generation must act now to ensure there's a better future for both the nation and gaia&quot; than &quot;Let's blow up more pipelines and kill as many CEOs we can get our paws on&quot;.<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/dXGG39V.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/dXGG39V.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/dXGG39V.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> MrornX, didn't we talked about spamming every conversation with WtE promotion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T17:00:39-07:00","id":1544759,"title":"","content":"The Quick Characters Chapter (Antagonists and Allies)<br /> <br /> One of the few places where it actually feels like a modern game, this chapter condenses stats heavily into broad categories and a few exceptional specifics. Regrettably, this means that Spirits were, like Garou, flattened utterly down to having fewer stats. Where the Garou lost Gnosis, the Spirits lost everything except... Power. Yeah, they're not really beating allegations that they didn't keep current on Werewolf stuff (we used Essence since Revised, thankyouverymuch).<br /> <br /> Spirits are the first on the docket for the chapter, which makes it seem like the Umbra chapter was longer, but they just cut the part detailing spirits out of it at some point and put it here. I suppose that works well enough.<br /> <br /> What isn't well enough is the book stopping to kick you, yet again, with some heavily Mage stuff about Garou having an &quot;imperfect understanding&quot; of the Umbra and possibly not knowing a bane from a non-corrupt spirit. While describing what a character perceives in sensory details is a general goal for running games a storyteller - showing rather than telling - the sidebar sounds like it's encouraging you to be a willfully malicious ass about it.<br /> <br /> Spirits only have Power as a stat, and some modifiers for Abilities or other actions. Spirits are also no longer capable of materializing; in a particularly &quot;BOO!&quot;-worthy passage, it poo-poos the idea of a Nexus Crawler emerging from the Umbra like a kaiju, and mentions that it instead temporarily possesses whatever is on hand - floors, tables, industrial equipment, etc. Banes are noted as being more capable in this arena, with long term possession resulting in fomori. I supposed it's doubtful that we'll be seeing gorgons or drones anytime soon.<br /> <br /> Everything that a spirit changes about its host disappears after it leaves. This is supposed to preserve the veil in the case of spirits not having physical bodies, but those faded from existence after no longer needed or when a spirit was physically defeated, so this isn't really a new thing, nor is it necessary to preserve the veil in the case of spirits actually building up physical bodies to act on the physical side of thing. Also spirits only reliably take agg from fire. Truly, this is the Promethean edition of Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Also, compare these two passages.<br /> <br /> [quote=Werewolf 20th Anniversary Edition]Banes are Wyrm-spirits, a collective name for the vast menagerie of spirit-minions at the Wyrm\u2019s command. Their forms are legion, each reflecting something of the particular aspect of the Wyrm that they serve. Most are foul of form, embodying the Wyrm\u2019s taint, but even this is no certainty. Destruction, deception, and corruption take<br /> many forms throughout the world, and if inhuman beauty and seemingly sweet seduction serves their Master\u2019s needs, some bane will surely reflect those \u201cvirtues.\u201d<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>W5</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the Garou, Banes are part of the vast menagerie of spirits that serve the Wyrm. Their forms are legion, each reflecting an aspect of that cosmological force. Most are grotesque, but many are subtler. Destruction, deception, and corruption take many forms, and if inhuman beauty and lustful seduction serve the Wyrm\u2019s needs, such is the face Banes present.</div> </div> </div> </div>That &quot;According to the Garou&quot; addendum is so fucking smarmy. \u200bI want to punch it. The book also seems to turn around and basically just copies the rest of what W20 had to say about them being wholly corrupt and malevolent. Does anyone else believe it's a reboot still? The only real difference is a fearful need to backpedal on every statement where it might be construed as standing for something, and also to dunk on animals that aren't humans - repeatedly, throughout this chapter, it regards them as &quot;lower order animals&quot;. I think only Freak Legion did that.<br /> <br /> Most of the banes are familiar, but I'm blanking on whether I've seen the Asklepian before under that name (it's a disease bane that spawns more of its kind of by infected other spirits and Garou).<br /> <br /> Bitter Rages are no longer in rare company in only temporarily possessing others, but they can make frenzies last as long as they want. Since you have to roll a potentially diminished temporary Willpower roll against half the bane's power, you'll probably need to get someone to help you kick one out unless you roll two 10s.<br /> <br /> Dissonant Gestalt is the only other new bane, basically one of organizational coverups and denial. The others are all quite familiar to anyone who's been playing for a while or who just got on board with W20. Some changes exist in odd places; humans possessed by scrags using guns, for example, or Wyrmholes not being able to possess hosts or throw down with their enemies. Nexus Crawlers got an awkward translation where they just decided that they should throw lots of dice at the characters instead of making the crawler weird and horrifying in what it does, as what it does can be resisted with Stamina + Occult now.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Wyld-spirits known as the Nameless have been drastically de-powered, and of course, there's no mention of their capability to cause a giant explosion by stripping something's name from it. Wouldn't be very street, I guess.<br /> <br /> Lunes still exist, and technically someone managed to use them to sneak moon bridges back in! It isn't quite instant, but being able to fast travel anywhere in a single night, provided you've placated the spirit, is a close second.<br /> <br /> Englings are still there, even though they no longer act as ways to regain Gnosis, because you don't have that Trait anymore. Now they just cause small miracles to happen, like fortuitous power outages or roots that your attacker trips on.<br /> <br /> Fomori powers changed a lot compared to past editions. Stomach Pumper is still there under a different name, they can still do toxic suicide attacks, but tentacles, instead of just being extra appendages, is now similar to said suicide attack; instead of chemicals, it erupts in an area effect grappling attack... which doesn't do the fomor much good if they can't grapple anymore on account of being dead.<br /> <br /> Pentex is there, as the Pentex Group. While I don't always agree with Justin Achilli, I do feel like it's not really necessary to keep it, but apparently in addition to all the classic banes this &quot;reboot&quot; needs it for some reason. I feel that giving it a Patron at all that wasn't a Corporate version of the City Father is a bad take, and selecting Fly for that role strikes me as something along the line of Gary Gygax hating hyenas and making gnolls to constantly harp on about how much he hates those filthy, ugly, disgusting hyenas while also writing for the game on the side, I guess. Seriously, unlike corporate executives, flies have an important role in supporting ecological webs. Fuck this game.<br /> <br /> Back to characters, the game starts to creep back into assuming you'll structure your chronicle into three acts, and gives an ascending threat level of operatives and employees that you'll meet early to late into the campaign. First Teams are also mentioned here, but srsly, you guys, it's totally a reboot. I feel that following a four act structure with reversals and upsets might better allow you to incorporate the equally twisting and labyrinthine politics of Pentex, or any other Wyrm-Influenced Corporation (WIC) into the mix, since rival board members might start supporting the pack with deniable assets. But then, I did technically come here from Shadowrun so many years ago, so...<br /> <br /> Using Garou as antagonists: the text box suggests not fully using the number of rolls that would be required to play a Garou as a PC. Gee, y'think? I don't even want to use all those rolls for PCs.<br /> <br /> The motivations given for the BSDs are far, far too charitable. Also, they're compared to accelerationists.<br /> <br /> The Cult of Fenris! I'd ask WTF the rest of the tribe of Wolf joined up with the Cult just for screaming louder, but I already know the answer. Also, this last part...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VV5</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some among Wolf\u2019s pledged, rather than follow their fellows, abandoned their Patron Spirit and pledged to other tribes. Trusting in the Patron Spirits to perceive any evidence of poor faith, the other tribes have accepted them, but being a former Wolf-pledged often earns Garou suspicion in their packs. Which, it must be admitted, is a very strange state in which werewolves find themselves: unable to trust Wolf.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not working, dudes. I'm not joining in one your angst parade. Also, the motivations ascribed to them are seeking a form of Valhalla. Let's face it; this isn't a reboot when shit like that slips out, setting aside that by Revised the Get would want to invade Valhalla to set it on fire and kill the Einherjar. Again.<br /> <br /> Some of the character details are also... oddly, perversely amusing. Like, the Ragabash is literally said to find joy in others' failures (schadenfraude!), or how the Ahroun is &quot;festooned with a variety of abhorrent symbols&quot;. I'm betting that the symbols are of a type that aren't considered abhorrent in India or East Asia, where they're associated with Buddha or the dead, but that's just going off of the general path from &quot;this is a continuation of the game!&quot; W5 from back in the early 2020s to the present &quot;this is a reboot, nay, a reimagining!&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, the theurge from the CoF has a rite that allows them to stop a character from regenerating. Having read through the system fully now, that seems crazy powerful, because Garou have very few good damage reduction powers and are absolutely dependent on regenerating damage constantly to not die.<br /> <br /> The Stargazers are the new Fianna, in that they are akin to Spinal Tap's take on the druids. No one knows where they came from, or what they were doing! <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aDTwO0TlwOU\" target=\"_blank\">BUY MY BOOK</a> to find out more whenever we decide to get on that!<br /> <br /> Stolen Moons - presented without credit to J. F. Sembrano! They constitute not just werewolves that have stolen skins to become werewolves, but also the indeterminately cursed and those who... (sigh deeper than in Track of the Moon Beast describing stew) made a deal with the devil.<br /> <br /> The Starving Remnant hints that disconnection and becoming a spirit in the Umbra when you die is a thing. But it takes a giant shit on the prospect of ancestor-spirits by basically just making it into a Garou spirit pulling a Ju-On to attack other werewolves.<br /> <br /> Raven-shifters won't shut up and have an eye for shinies. No fucking way is this not supposed to be the W:tA of old.<br /> <br /> Spider-shifters get a break on being able to use Sacred Territory; they can just shot web. No need to unzip or cut yourself (or... both?) when you don't have sacred caern water to spill for a temporary boost.<br /> <br /> The section on vampires opens up with a Garou talking about how they're an infestation in cities. Doesn't seem like anyone who was claiming that Garou and Kindred could be friends were really reading this book, honestly. Two vampire antagonists, one of each of the other games from the Big Five, with the fae being presented as some kind of super-edgy fishmalk.<br /> <br /> We get normal threats. Breaking a WoD tradition, cops aren't given borderline superhuman stats. Well, maybe the IAO or SAD. I'm not quite sure where the IAO is going to place spy devices where a being who can arbitrarily control technology isn't going to find them, though. And for Glass Walkers? Fuhgeddaboutit!<br /> <br /> Animals as antagonists - I'll at least give the text that it's good to consult groups before using them, since fighting off beasts in the forests like some kind of early level hack RPG grindfest is not a thing that most probably take well. Wolves are mentioned first, and... have exactly the same stats as great cats. Do... do the people working on this game know that tigers are closer to bear size than wolf size? Also, someone forgot to give them good Survival stats; animals all get 1 for social and mental actions that don't involve intimidation, which is right out. No one's going to be rolling Academics, but there's often a wide variety of social effectiveness in groups of social animals (such as wolves), and spotting traps for an animal that has experience with humans is a common capability (just ask anyone with very stubborn community cats). We also get swarm mechanics, for treating larger groups of small animals or other beings as a single target with a single health level track.<br /> <br /> Oh, since bears have higher Physical pools than great cats or wolves, they also get a higher sneaking dice pool. This is actually closer to real life than you might think; Golden Kamuy could rattle on about bears being tricky all day, but at the very least, they are among the animals that will backtrack if you're following them.<br /> <br /> Next time: I dress down how W5 handles loresheets and provide counter examples of how I would have expected them to be done!<br /> <br /> Tying up loose ends about Shadows and the Umbra: The descriptions of the Umbra from past editions always started describing the Umbra as a shadow, but then referred to it as a reflection. I think the sudden jump in the metaphor was useful in illustrating that you're not dealing with something that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T17:03:04-07:00","id":1544760,"title":"","content":"... (Continuing from unfinished last paragraph rather than risking an edit): exists in real life experience. It knows that the metaphor is going to break down and plans for it; W5 thinks that it's too clever to fail and so <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2WZLJpMOxS4\" target=\"_blank\">never sees the rakes coming</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T18:25:30-07:00","id":1544827,"title":"","content":"Loresheets! They're supposed to connect the character to the greater WoD. They work like Backgrounds, so they kind of fall through at certain levels. What do we get?<br /> <br /> Monkeywrenchers: Go from swaying crowds to setting fires to throwing parties to finding scapegoats to making another monkeywrencher a scapegoat once per story in exchange for pinning something definitively on Pentex. I think they lost the plot somewhere, since most presentations of monkeywrenching that I recall were a wee but subtler, involving deep cover infiltration and information drops. This is definitely a pessimistic take on the act and practice of being a monkeywrencher, in keeping with its &quot;nothing matters, you can't win&quot; attempts to wrench angst from the reader.<br /> <br /> Project Twilight: What the Monkeywrencher was trying to be, but with the FBI's monster-hunting SAD. You're like Marsha Crowe from the original book, but instead of Kinfolk posted to monitor it, you're a full-on werewolf. You know, if the Garou could do this, how did they lose? This allows you to cover up shit, distort the truth, and potentially sic the agency on your enemies. Inconsistent with many of the presentations of the world, to be sure, but haven't you wanted to sit back and laugh while SAD cooperates with the SI to take down a vampire?<br /> <br /> Umbral Traveler: This shouldn't be a Background. This should be the default for how you interact with the Umbra. This is like Day 1 DLC fixing a broken Umbra to allow you to, you know, survive it and actually use it in a chronicle.<br /> <br /> Renunciate of Fenris: You were caught in the editor's temper tantrum between editions. Much like Umbral Traveler, this is Day 1 DLC in some cases, like being the only system that allows you to avoid being counted out from accumulating too much Hauglosk. The first dot, though, is just insulting, as it describes your character as liking the taste of leather.<br /> <br /> The Black Spiral: The infamous &quot;I guess those Spirals aren't so bad, after all!&quot; Loresheet, as the ceiling level allows you to deprogram BSDs. I can only assume that Mage will allow you to redeem Nephandi like Jodi Blake after just three days. The other levels are like Wyrm Lore from older editions, only instead of risking insanity, you're risking a hit to your reputation.<br /> <br /> So, what's my problem with these as Loresheets? Well, in Weapons of the Gods, where Ken Hite got this concept from for V5, Loresheets had a wildly variable cost and effect, or set of them. As such, I'm of the opinion that Backgrounds were the wrong way to go, and that they should have been merits, as long as you're using both by default. Secondly, as noted, some of these are just restoring prior functionality instead of actually building up to something, especially with the mountain of lore that W:tA has. If it seems overwhelming to others, you can slow drip it to people in the form of Loresheets, kind of like how WotG manages to ease you into its setting (as well as cultural background information, for those unfamiliar with Chinese history and culture or the genres of wuxia and xianxia).<br /> <br /> This would have been the perfect place to cram in the various prominent ancestor-spirits featured in Rage, for example. Or talismans, you remember those? They have legends associated with them; they aren't just equipment with better plusses. By making them Merits and detailing various facets of the setting, you could use Loresheets to get engagement with any portion of the setting, zero in on one corner of the lore as your Chronicle's focus, set up conflicts for your character that are narratively interesting... and they use it as fucking Day 1 DLC. Well, I suppose that's a classic PDX move, but still, what a waste.<br /> <br /> How I would make it work:<br /> <br /> Project Twilight (*)<br /> Many among the Garou Nation attempt to place moles in human agencies and other places of power, but you have actually managed it, passing all background checks and avoiding too much suspicion to sit right within the belly of the beast as a SAD agent. You will need to keep up with typical work expected of a federal investigator, but if you have a supernatural method of sharing thoughts and information, you can keep your pack or handler abreast of SAD operations and potentially steer them away from any incidences involving werewolves, at least before anyone can clean up, without any the wiser.<br /> <br /> *-**** Rank: The default assumption is that your ranking in SAD is as a junior agent. By paying more merit dots, you can increase your seniority, up to the point of being its director. Talk with your ST to determine how far placed your chronicle can see you.<br /> <br /> *+: Armory: Equivalent to your standing, you can requisition potentially valuable items from the SAD armory, potentially including devices that are effective against vampires or other threats in the dark. Normally, these must reside in and be returned to the holding location, or else the character risks scrutiny.<br /> <br /> *** Raid: After spending several sessions during the story researching a threat, the character can arrange for the target of this scrutiny to suffer a raid by the agency's primary combatants. Such agents will be armed and armored, with whatever countermeasures SAD possesses against it if the party is known to be a &quot;strange threat&quot; off the books. Note that while this can be an incredible weapon against some threats, its usefulness is limited against very old vampires, archmages and other figures of power, or large concentrations of beings that can easily take on an agent one on one, such as Black Spiral hives. It is also ill-advised to try it against corrupting threats like the Chulorviah, who can infect agents participating in the raid and turn them into the Enfolded.<br /> <br /> ****: Top Secret: You have security clearance to know whatever US federal law enforcement knows about the supernatural; if you are below an appropriately senior rank, you must come up with a good reason for this alongside your ST, such as through a &quot;Deep Throat&quot; or &quot;Mr. X&quot; figure. This allows you to roll again to discern something about another monster if you fail your roll.<br /> <br /> Or consider a legendary ancestor-spirit...<br /> <br /> Leukippes<br /> A Scythian before her First Change and life in the Black Furies, Leukippes is widely known as a rider, warrior, and archer, but tales also speak of her cunning and subtlety in approaching overwhelming threats.<br /> <br /> ** You descend strongly from Leukippes, either by blood or martial tradition. You gain +1 to Athletics and +1 to Firearms when calling upon Leukippes via Ancestors in addition to any other Traits.<br /> <br /> ***: Descending strongly from Leukippes, you may, once per game, bypass a set of foolproof security measures via disguise. This will get you past an impassible obstacle in order to get within the reach of an enemy that you have spent the past few game sessions learning about from observations or witnesses; whatever happens after you and your pack are through and clear is thereafter up to your collective capabilities as a pack.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps...<br /> <br /> Kailindo (A system topic) **<br /> <br /> Trained by Stargazers or Galestalkers in shapeshifting as easily as if you were made of the wind, you can engage in a number of special combat techniques, with each requiring a Rage check per dot of rating.<br /> <br /> * Subtle Breeze<br /> ** Growing Tempest<br /> *** Melting Wind<br /> **** Striking the Wind<br /> ***** The Hurricane<br /> <br /> (That last one looks like it could be a background, but a lot of fighting styles cut out before that, and some went on for several more.)<br /> <br /> I could go on and probably fill a book the size of WotG with them. W5 probably wouldn't want to avow the existence of any of the legendary fetishes from Hammer and Klaive, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T10:27:22-07:00","id":1544854,"title":"","content":"I would just like to add, that in my own extensive review of W5 that I posted here earlier this year, I mentioned how a few other problems: the lack of crediting the creators of earlier editions on the credit page; a sidebar in the Umbra chapter on how only the Garou can visit the Umbra, other splats have their own sections of the Otherworlds, and if any of them could get to the Spirit Wilds, they wouldn't experience the same things; and an unusual typo in the index of where &quot;Gaia&quot; is capitalized in one instance, but not another, showing how each entry was probably entered in at different times. I could go on, but it would just be easier to find the closed thread yourselves. (I am not good at adding links. Sorry.)<br /> <br /> I will add that many of the 'problems' with W5 seem stem from the lack of time to finish writing and editing it before the self-imposed deadline. The designers seemed to have particular ideas in mind in 'correcting' the problems with previous editions. While they did manage to make those changes, other portions were left incomplete. It feels like they were following a video game model, where important additions would come in later forms, for the about the same amount of money; instead of the traditional TTRPG model where such material would be more 'optional' in nature.<br /> <br /> What gets me is that when the information about W5 was first released about two years ago, I was able to come up with metaplot explanations for many of the changes that afternoon, without the help of looking at any of the previous material. Yet, after many years, the designers felt that they had to start over from scratch to get to the same points. I could give a lengthy rundown, but one example should be enough.<br /> <br /> For instance, the current generation of Garou don't trust their history because it is mostly oral, and 'everyone knows' how untrustworthy that can be. Many W5 fans defend this saying it allows them to make up their own histories, something that fans have always been allowed to do. These fans also gloss over the fact that it could be hiding that the design team ran out of time to figure out what to keep and how to interpret it. Short, simple, and very quick.<br /> <br /> My take: During the lead-up events to the Last Battle, the Garou Nation found out that the Silver Record was a reproduction, the original destroyed by the White Howlers when they emerged as the BSD. A critical prophecy was needed, but had been lost due to this, and it needed to be recreated. In the distant past, the Garou asked each Tribe to send in some of their own records to recreate the Record. However, this was incomplete, as each Tribe redacted portions that they felt shown their Tribe in a bad light, leaving a widely biased form of most of the histories. Even then, the Record is barely 20% the size it was then, even with the modern additions included in the centuries since. A entire cross-Tribal camp was created to prevent anyone finding out that the Record was destroyed, save for a few Elders every generation. Those kept out of the loop included the Keeper. When the Stargazers joined, they revealed that a complete version still existed, in the High Umbra. Thus began a campaign to discourage Garou to enter there. The entire story comes out when one of the Elders reveals it when the need for the missing prophecy becomes too great. While that aided in the Last Battle, the current generation of Garou distrusts anything about the histories, even those events that occurred later, especially after a rouge member of the camp does something to prevent anyone in finding the Record in the High Umbra.<br /> <br /> Yes, my way is much longer, but it easily connects to existing lore, even in this shortened version presented here. It still leads to a suspicion of the past, but in a way that just barely stretches the imagination, in a way that W5 does not. I did this for many of the changes found in W5, even with changes to past lore. Now, if I could do that without looking at any of the older material, with the majority outline being made in a few hours, someone with access to every book ever made and many years could have done the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T11:44:22-07:00","id":1544859,"title":"","content":"Self-imposed a deadline as &quot;Get it out by Gen Con!&quot; might have been, they'd have plenty of time to do it if they hired an editor that wasn't hellbent on trying to make the game as unpleasant as possible at every turn.<br /> <br /> Speaking personally, I'd be hesitant to try and approach a &quot;no one trusts the history&quot; plot on account of how I get tired out with that kind of thing on the internet with conspiracy theories and all. A lot of the metaplot is from the BNS LARP for Werewolf, too, which is like an entirely different game with vastly different needs. As we saw, those details just didn't fit with the tabletop version of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T12:06:24-07:00","id":1544860,"title":"","content":"With &quot;self-imposed deadline&quot; I would think more about Justin Achilli as the lead-developer leaving before work on the W5 corebook was finished. In retrospect, wasn't it awfully convenient that the writing-process was considered finished just right before he left in January 2023 and <i>immediately </i>switched to his new job somewhere else? Especially considering the way Justin described things in October 2022 they only had finished work on the Antagonist-section as far as writing was concerned. Who knows what went on behind the scenes there but that's certainly not how all of this is supposed to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T12:41:51-07:00","id":1544863,"title":"","content":"And they decided that an adventure with pretty much no characters who are established or who stick around, or are memorable at all, was a substitute for the past editions' section on the Sept of the Green. At least go the rest of the way lying about the nature of the reboot and convert that setting and its characters, too.<br /> <br /> (That is also my review of the adventure, with the added note of &quot;This feels a lot like a railroad. Why would you do that in this day and age?&quot; I really just couldn't get through it. Maybe I can try later, but it's definitely not something that I feel even has useful parts for cannibalizing into my own thing. Note that the irony of saying that along with the meat puppet featuring into the adventure are not lost on me.)<br /> <br /> ((Also for a game that tries to make sure that everyone is on board with the material in an adventure, there's a high chance, given what gets most peoples' goats, that what features into this one is going to make it so that it doesn't get used, anyway.))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T03:52:36-07:00","id":1544883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544827#post1544827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what's my problem with these as Loresheets? Well, in Weapons of the Gods, where Ken Hite got this concept from for V5, Loresheets had a wildly variable cost and effect, or set of them. As such, I'm of the opinion that Backgrounds were the wrong way to go, and that they should have been merits, as long as you're using both by default. Secondly, as noted, some of these are just restoring prior functionality instead of actually building up to something, especially with the mountain of lore that W:tA has. If it seems overwhelming to others, you can slow drip it to people in the form of Loresheets, kind of like how WotG manages to ease you into its setting (as well as cultural background information, for those unfamiliar with Chinese history and culture or the genres of wuxia and xianxia).<br /> <br /> This would have been the perfect place to cram in the various prominent ancestor-spirits featured in Rage, for example. Or talismans, you remember those? They have legends associated with them; they aren't just equipment with better plusses. By making them Merits and detailing various facets of the setting, you could use Loresheets to get engagement with any portion of the setting, zero in on one corner of the lore as your Chronicle's focus, set up conflicts for your character that are narratively interesting... and they use it as fucking Day 1 DLC. Well, I suppose that's a classic PDX move, but still, what a waste.</div> </div> </div> </div>To come back to the Loresheets, it's a near miracle that the W5 corebook ended up with any Loresheets. I'm always thinking of that section in the V5 Players Guide about Loresheets:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Loresheets exist to highlight a certain aspect of the world for the interested player and Storyteller,\u200b without forcing every player to master the entire minutiae of the Vampire setting. A Loresheet foregrounds some group, historical event, or elder <b>as it relates specifically to the player</b>, encouraging them to take ownership of that aspect and reminding the Storyteller that vampiric arcana exists to serve the story at the table tonight, not as mandatory history lessons.\u200b </div> </div> </div>(Emphasis from the book)<br /> <br /> They didn't put all the Loresheets from the OP books into the V5 Players Guide and the H5 corebook launched with no Loresheets at all. Instead of figuring out how to use Loresheets and make them part of a game like H5, they simply didn't use them. It's only now many years later that the upcoming Apostates supplement starts to think about what Loresheets in H5 look like. As there was little to no desire to engage with Loresheets as a tool, it's no surprise that they ended up being this weird mix of various things with no bigger idea of how they're supposed to fit into the game. They had a real attitude of &quot;The best number of Loresheets to use in a WOD5E game is zero.&quot; back then.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Umbral Traveler: This shouldn't be a Background. This should be the default for how you interact with the Umbra. This is like Day 1 DLC fixing a broken Umbra to allow you to, you know, survive it and actually use it in a chronicle. </div> </div> </div>This one's especially odd. The boni are very weird. Take the first dot &quot;The Difficulty to return to the physical world from the Umbra by using the Rite of Shadow Passage is reduced by 1 when you\u2019re the Rite master (see p. 180).\u200b&quot; But here's what it already states in Rite of the Shadow Passage: &quot;The Difficulty to return to the physical world from the Umbra using this Rite is reduced by 2\u200b\u200b.&quot; This has the feeling of the left hand not knowing what the right hand was doing.<br /> <br /> And then the other boni are also strangely constrained. Like whenever an effect is described, somebody felt the need to add a cautious &quot;But...&quot; to it as if the writer feared making the dots <i>too </i>good.<br /> <br /> Second dot: You can attract the attention of pattern spiders... once per scene... if they are present... and they don't necessarily like you.<br /> Third dot: You can see ghosts in the Umbra and in the real world - unless they use powers to hide from you. And you can communicate with them - unless they don't want to talk to you.<br /> Fourth dot: A very good one! You only take superficial damage when you run out of WP in the Umbra.<br /> Fifth dot: You know some sort of &quot;monumental secret&quot; about the Umbra - except &quot;whatever puissant spirit the secret is about knows you know.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Black Spiral: The infamous &quot;I guess those Spirals aren't so bad, after all!&quot; Loresheet, as the ceiling level allows you to deprogram BSDs. I can only assume that Mage will allow you to redeem Nephandi like Jodi Blake after just three days. The other levels are like Wyrm Lore from older editions, only instead of risking insanity, you're risking a hit to your reputation. </div> </div> </div>I am curious how they're gonna handle Black Spiral Dancers in the next W5 supplement, Wyrmtide. They're still supposed to be antagonists but this Loresheet really set up the template of them being more like misguided bad boys that aren't that bad after you get to know them. Tellingly this isn't a Loresheet about how you study this one type of enemy and get better at taking them out. It's about how you hang out with them and know their lingo. And the ultimate ability is to talk someone out of being a Black Spiral Dancer...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T05:57:26-07:00","id":1544884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544883#post1544883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious how they're gonna handle Black Spiral Dancers in the next W5 supplement, Wyrmtide. They're still supposed to be antagonists but this Loresheet really set up the template of them being more like misguided bad boys that aren't that bad after you get to know them. Tellingly this isn't a Loresheet about how you study this one type of enemy and get better at taking them out. It's about how you hang out with them and know their lingo. And the ultimate ability is to talk someone out of being a Black Spiral Dancer...</div> </div> </div> </div>And THEN Shattered Nation doubles down on that, instead of showcasing WHY one might want to leave a BSD life in the first place.<br /> <br /> As someone who likes the tribe (both 20th ed and previous version), this is doing so much harm to the horror they bring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T06:29:49-07:00","id":1544886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544883#post1544883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To come back to the Loresheets, it's a near miracle that the W5 corebook ended up with any Loresheets. I'm always thinking of that section in the V5 Players Guide about Loresheets:<br /> <br /> <br /> (Emphasis from the book)<br /> <br /> They didn't put all the Loresheets from the OP books into the V5 Players Guide and the H5 corebook launched with no Loresheets at all. Instead of figuring out how to use Loresheets and make them part of a game like H5, they simply didn't use them. It's only now many years later that the upcoming Apostates supplement starts to think about what Loresheets in H5 look like. As there was little to no desire to engage with Loresheets as a tool, it's no surprise that they ended up being this weird mix of various things with no bigger idea of how they're supposed to fit into the game. They had a real attitude of &quot;The best number of Loresheets to use in a WOD5E game is zero.&quot; back then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess Hite's design sensibilities didn't mesh well with someone else's. A pity; it's a good way to set up characters with connections to the world. Just as long as your ST isn't being a complete jerk about what they want to do and trying to keep PCs out of any kind of influence or importance ohhhhh... I think I get why.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This one's especially odd. The boni are very weird. Take the first dot &quot;The Difficulty to return to the physical world from the Umbra by using the Rite of Shadow Passage is reduced by 1 when you\u2019re the Rite master (see p. 180).&quot; But here's what it already states in Rite of the Shadow Passage: &quot;The Difficulty to return to the physical world from the Umbra using this Rite is reduced by 2\u200b\u200b.&quot; This has the feeling of the left hand not knowing what the right hand was doing. </div> </div> </div>I thought that it would stack, but with this game, who knows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And then the other boni are also strangely constrained. Like whenever an effect is described, somebody felt the need to add a cautious &quot;But...&quot; to it as if the writer feared making the dots <i>too </i>good.<br /> <br /> Second dot: You can attract the attention of pattern spiders... once per scene... if they are present... and they don't necessarily like you.<br /> Third dot: You can see ghosts in the Umbra and in the real world - unless they use powers to hide from you. And you can communicate with them - unless they don't want to talk to you.<br /> Fourth dot: A very good one! You only take superficial damage when you run out of WP in the Umbra.<br /> Fifth dot: You know some sort of &quot;monumental secret&quot; about the Umbra - except &quot;whatever puissant spirit the secret is about knows you know.\u200b&quot; </div> </div> </div>Everything but the fourth dot just seems like padding. Like the Storm Warden merit from Mage Revised, with lots of extra steps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am curious how they're gonna handle Black Spiral Dancers in the next W5 supplement, Wyrmtide. They're still supposed to be antagonists but this Loresheet really set up the template of them being more like misguided bad boys that aren't that bad after you get to know them. Tellingly this isn't a Loresheet about how you study this one type of enemy and get better at taking them out. It's about how you hang out with them and know their lingo. And the ultimate ability is to talk someone out of being a Black Spiral Dancer... </div> </div> </div>Normally, the end result is the other way around. Truly, this is a backwards crazy edition of W:tA. &quot;Learn Wyrm Lore. If your level in the Knowledge is higher than your Willpower, remove a derangement from target BSD character.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T10:25:48-07:00","id":1544892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544886#post1544886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Normally, the end result is the other way around. Truly, this is a backwards crazy edition of W:tA. &quot;Learn Wyrm Lore. If your level in the Knowledge is higher than your Willpower, remove a derangement from target BSD character.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's horrible! It's like saying the BSD are evil because they are insane! It's like a return to that idea that &quot;people with mental conditions are evil.&quot;<br /> <br /> Do you not know this guy who wants to kill you and your people? Ends, they are just crazy, because, you know, crazy people are evil, but sane people are good, never evil. So, if you fix how this mind works, then all be fine!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T13:04:22-07:00","id":1544910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544892#post1544892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's horrible! It's like saying the BSD are evil because they are insane! It's like a return to that idea that &quot;people with mental conditions are evil.&quot;<br /> <br /> Do you not know this guy who wants to kill you and your people? Ends, they are just crazy, because, you know, crazy people are evil, but sane people are good, never evil. So, if you fix how this mind works, then all be fine!</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't even just that, by making BSDs of all things more positive they are only making the bias against the Fenrir more clear. Because CoF, despite being on Gaia's side, are NOT given any such leeway.<br /> <br /> It makes this unbalanced setting, where hanging out with polluting tainted monsters is better than those who want to dedicate their life to the fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T13:28:03-07:00","id":1544918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544910#post1544910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It isn't even just that, by making BSDs of all things more positive they are only making the bias against the Fenrir more clear. Because CoF, despite being on Gaia's side, are NOT given any such leeway.<br /> <br /> It makes this unbalanced setting, where hanging out with polluting tainted monsters is better than those who want to dedicate their life to the fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, there is that rare capacity for beating back Hauglosk at 4, maybe. Then you can transfer your Hauglosk into Harano and lose your character, just as the editor intended!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T15:53:05-07:00","id":1544933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544918#post1544918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, there is that rare capacity for beating back Hauglosk at 4, maybe. Then you can transfer your Hauglosk into Harano and lose your character, just as the editor intended!</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean also Hauglosk seems to lock you into being a ecofash or at least belligerent dick, Like at least give us some verity like making a werewolf version of don quixote who's actions stems from doing what they preseaves as good deeds, but are hampered by the fact that he's ultimately viewing reality from extremely warped prestictive. <br /> <br /> Also funnily enough Hauglosk into Harano could actually simulate how Don Quixote bing crushed by cruel reality in the end of the second book and went into a deep depression and ultimately died because of it. Although Man of Lamacha has a slightly happier ending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T16:49:47-07:00","id":1544940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544933#post1544933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean also Hauglosk seems to lock you into being a ecofash or at least belligerent dick, Like at least give us some verity like making a werewolf version of don quixote who's actions stems from doing what they preseaves as good deeds, but are hampered by the fact that he's ultimately viewing reality from extremely warped prestictive.<br /> <br /> Also funnily enough Hauglosk into Harano could actually simulate how Don Quixote bing crushed by cruel reality in the end of the second book and went into a deep depression and ultimately died because of it. Although Man of Lamacha has a slightly happier ending.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, we're talking about W5. It'd almost have to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T18:48:47-07:00","id":1544949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544940#post1544940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, we're talking about W5. It'd almost have to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>This quote basically sums up all of W5's problems The garou always have to screw up. They always has to lose and they always has to be miserable. Like RPG is about the player making choices and changing the setting through the actions of they characters.<br /> <br /> While W5 basically spent half it's page lecturing the players on how that's childish and they should act like gown adult. While playing a game that in a medium that basically consists of people ment to be around the adult age range sitting around a table and playing make beleave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T23:48:28-07:00","id":1544952,"title":"","content":"Two things occur about the surpringly soft approach to the spirals.<br /> <br /> 1) spirals as historically enthusiastic rapists amoung other horrific crimes to a degree which is personally irredeemable for most people irl.<br /> <br /> 2) the cult of fenris are definatly not getting this soft touch approach.<br /> <br /> while this #notallspirals approach could be interesting in terms of re interpretation. Its very odd considering the absolutist approach with the get.<br /> <br /> Atm the cult feel like the authors are overcompensating to try and sell them as baddies to the detriment of the overall writting and this becomes really jarring with the historically repulsive spiral dancers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-29T03:00:18-07:00","id":1544959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544884#post1544884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And THEN Shattered Nation doubles down on that, instead of showcasing WHY one might want to leave a BSD life in the first place.<br /> <br /> As someone who likes the tribe (both 20th ed and previous version), this is doing so much harm to the horror they bring.</div> </div> </div> </div>The part that had me really go &quot;Wait, what?&quot; is when you get this from Shattered Nation (pg 117):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some Dancers invoke old agreements made with the White Howlers, claiming themselves as direct descendants. It has happened that these agreements are honored by a sept in hopes that they can use them to keep the Wyrm adherents in check or seek a way to bring them back to the Garou. It\u2019s probably unsurprising that such a choice is massively controversial among the Garou. </div> </div> </div>Not only does that contradict the idea that present-day Garou know barely anything about their history but it also continues this trend in W5 where the BSD are just &quot;misunderstood bad boys&quot; that at the end of the day just mean well. You get to the last sentence in that quoted passage there and you might think at the start &quot;Ah, yes, 'It's probably unsurprising...'. They're going to talk about how BSD are these dangerous psychopaths and Wyrm-fanatics. And that's why it's bad to trust them even when it's comforting to buy into that rhetoric during the Age of Apocalypse.&quot;. But no, how it actually ends is to just call the idea of allying with BSD &quot;controversial&quot;. It's just more &quot;misunderstood bad guys&quot;-stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-29T06:51:35-07:00","id":1544968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544952#post1544952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Atm the cult feel like the authors are overcompensating to try and sell them as baddies to the detriment of the overall writting and this becomes really jarring with the historically repulsive spiral dancers.</div> </div> </div> </div>They very much are harming their own product with this. By making CoF such untouchable tribe that they have NOTHING positive to them (even BSDs in 1st ed had many positives over garou nation) and there is zero chance to reason with them, they are also making so every other faction looks good in comparison. Which might work IF this wasn't WtA and if one of those tribes wasn't the BSDs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-29T07:39:31-07:00","id":1544973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544959#post1544959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not only does that contradict the idea that present-day Garou know barely anything about their history but it also continues this trend in W5 where the BSD are just &quot;misunderstood bad boys&quot; that at the end of the day just mean well. You get to the last sentence in that quoted passage there and you might think at the start &quot;Ah, yes, 'It's probably unsurprising...'. They're going to talk about how BSD are these dangerous psychopaths and Wyrm-fanatics. And that's why it's bad to trust them even when it's comforting to buy into that rhetoric during the Age of Apocalypse.&quot;. But no, how it actually ends is to just call the idea of allying with BSD &quot;controversial&quot;. It's just more &quot;misunderstood bad guys&quot;-stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heere's a question the writers did not ask; Why should they try to convert the BSDs back to Gaia? If the ruling philosophy of W5 is that the Nation is gone and everyone can do what they want, then what are the BSDs doing wrong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-29T08:24:41-07:00","id":1544980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544973#post1544973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heere's a question the writers did not ask; Why should they try to convert the BSDs back to Gaia? If the ruling philosophy of W5 is that the Nation is gone and everyone can do what they want, then what are the BSDs doing wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially in the context of the Ghost Council and the Red Talons. The former is all about &quot;the ends justify the means&quot; and that includes allying with the Wyrm to overcome whatever the opposition is. Meanwhile, with the latter you have this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the point of view of other werewolves from the now-shattered Garou Nation, the Red Talon perspective borders on the heretical. Red Talons often think that it isn\u2019t the Wyrm that\u2019s the imbalanced element of the Triat, but rather the Weaver, with its ever-expanding restrictiveness and malignant expansion in the form of cities, development, and \u201ccivilization.\u201d Among the most extreme of Red Talons \u2014 even expressing such a sentiment is shameful \u2014 the Wyrm is a victim of the Weaver, and the Wyrm\u2019s tools have their place. </div> </div> </div>Once you get past &quot;The Garou-Nation has fallen&quot;, &quot;It's the Age of Apocalypse.&quot; and you get to descriptions like this one, why wouldn't BSD just be another bunch of Garou indistinguishable from the playable Tribes...?<br /> <br /> The text is trying so hard to be dismissive and complain about the Garou that you get to a point where you just start to wonder &quot;Does any of this even matter if all of it sucks this much...?&quot;. Why would you even give a shit about Garou traditions and Gaia being dead/dying if nothing in Garou society works and all of their goals, hopes and dreams are categorically unachievable? At that point, why wouldn't you look at Packs of werewolves in W5 as just a bunch of marauders traveling through a wasteland rather than these firm, organized ideological factions? But since W5 isn't willing to take that leap of faith and leave pretty much all of the WtA-premise behind (despite the developers' strategy to &quot;redecorate&quot; the WtA-setting using a sledgehammer), the standard for &quot;good&quot; in the setting remains unimaginative traditionalism. You just gotta get that caern and wait for the Apocalypse in it. There's nothing else you can do in W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-29T09:19:33-07:00","id":1544989,"title":"","content":"&quot;Borderline heretical&quot; in a game where two tribes were called urrah for loving city life. Meanwhile, in legacy, it was such a cold take that there was an entire scenario of Apocalypse dedicated to how the Weaver will kill you. Again, it's just a rotten re-take of Revised with a lot of pieces missing, written by people who think that wolves can pass as dogs (HA HA! CLEMENT LUPUS!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-29T09:51:58-07:00","id":1544996,"title":"","content":"The problem is that when you combine watering down the evil of the BSD with also making &quot;heretical&quot; beliefs among the playable Garou Tribes a more common thing, then you get this morally grey soup where no ideological position matters all that much. &quot;So you're a Red Talon Garou who believes the Weaver is the true enemy and that's why you intentionally spread plagues...?&quot; - according to W5 that's a concept for a PC. On the other hand, you can have a Pack of BSD trying to reclaim a caern that was formerly held by the White Howlers and who are also willing to fight against Pentex to claim that caern - according to W5 that's a valid story-concept. After the waters have been muddied like that, ideological questions become far more individualized and heavily depend on the circumstances at the moment. Just because a Garou tells you that they think the Weaver is worse than the Wyrm doesn't make them automatically a bad guy, for example, in this kind of setting. If anything, getting that granular about the setting in W5's context turns into a bit of a nothingburger. Gaia's dead/dying, it's the Age of Apocalypse, the Garou Nation has fallen... why would you even bother getting invested in some grand theory of why things are the way they are? You're playing out the immediate aftermath of a fuck-up of epic proportions. (Although it doesn't help that the worldbuilding and accompanying writing in the W5 corebook leave a lot to be desired...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-29T18:47:07-07:00","id":1545027,"title":"","content":"In the end, I'm only left wondering this - can I disruptively introduce legacy lore via Loresheets into STV? Because it'd be difficult to work with the Background format, but I could still try. Before even getting any WoD5 books, I was even sketching up a Loresheet that implies that the character with it had been through the events of Shattered Dreams, and remembered it even if no one but Chronos and some other higher-tier spirits did. Given how the ParaWolf team treated it, I figured it would be as close to revenge as is attainable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-29T19:56:00-07:00","id":1545031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1545027#post1545027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, I'm only left wondering this - can I disruptively introduce legacy lore via Loresheets into STV? Because it'd be difficult to work with the Background format, but I could still try. Before even getting any WoD5 books, I was even sketching up a Loresheet that implies that the character with it had been through the events of Shattered Dreams, and remembered it even if no one but Chronos and some other higher-tier spirits did. Given how the ParaWolf team treated it, I figured it would be as close to revenge as is attainable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or even better just recton the whole setting taking place in the beta test of Lycanthrope: the Rapture online and the adventure that comes with involves resuing all the trapped garou souls that powers the games serves or at least putting them out of they misery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 10-30-2024, 06:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T18:18:26-07:00","id":1545183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1545031#post1545031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or even better just recton the whole setting taking place in the beta test of Lycanthrope: the Rapture online and the adventure that comes with involves resuing all the trapped garou souls that powers the games serves or at least putting them out of they misery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid that I don't have the stomach for making it into an over the top self-parody that wouldn't be out of place in the last chapter of Subsidiaries. I'm talking about being the Nightshade of W5 - get people so used to legacy lore that the attempts to get rid of it fall flat, or are at least mired in a fandom schism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-02T22:59:55-08:00","id":1548130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543084-a-legacy-fan-finally-reads-w5?p=1544854#post1544854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For instance, the current generation of Garou don't trust their history because it is mostly oral, and 'everyone knows' how untrustworthy that can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as you ignore how oral records can be insanely accurate, to the point the Australian Aboriginal oral tradition goes back 10k years to startingly accurate detail, such as describing the exact position of a star when Tasmania became an island due to rising sea levels, or how lakes formed around then active volcanos, or how their songlines can accurately guide a person across thousands of kilometers. W5 really doesn't seem to respect anything outside the anglo-sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}